","aliases":["First Impressionist exhibition"],"photos":[],"questionIds":["GEN43-Q03745"],"tapestryIds":["t68-0aa5f3ada6ca"],"museumIds":[],"mapIds":[],"note":"Independent exhibition in Paris; the movement's label developed from critical responses.","creator":"Claude Monet, Edgar Degas, Berthe Morisot, Camille Pissarro, Pierre-Auguste Renoir"},{"id":"LE102-622c2c837c0bb57b","title":"Woman with a Parasol","kind":"art","reference":"https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?search=Woman%20with%20a%20Parasol","aliases":["Woman with a Parasol"],"photos":[{"src":"/.netlify/functions/access?action=media&name=e210eec748020e9e04483e92.webp","credit":"Claude Monet","license":"Public domain","sourceUrl":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Claude_Monet_-_Woman_with_a_Parasol_-_Madame_Monet_and_Her_Son_-_Google_Art_Project.jpg","caption":"Identified work. Sculpture photographs may show later casts or surviving copies."},{"src":"/.netlify/functions/access?action=media&name=e210eec748020e9e04483e92.webp","credit":"Claude Monet","license":"Public domain","sourceUrl":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Claude_Monet_-_Woman_with_a_Parasol_-_Madame_Monet_and_Her_Son_-_Google_Art_Project.jpg","licenseUrl":""}],"questionIds":["GEN43-Q01239"],"tapestryIds":["t68-4c0712eec1a6"],"museumIds":[],"mapIds":[],"note":"The 1875 canvas depicts Camille and Jean Monet; do not confuse it with later parasol paintings.","creator":"Claude Monet","assetIds":["T81-t68-4c0712eec1a6"]},{"id":"LE102-8bde5182e4a9c1b0","title":"Bell's telephone patent","kind":"history","reference":"https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?search=Bell%27s%20telephone%20patent","aliases":["Bell's telephone patent"],"photos":[],"questionIds":["ARCHED-NEW101-0490","ARCHED-NEW101-0526"],"tapestryIds":["t68-8b1557f5190c"],"museumIds":[],"mapIds":[],"note":"A milestone in telephone development; multiple inventors contributed to the technology."},{"id":"LE102-b79d5949b0c0c2fb","title":"Dance at Le Moulin de la Galette","kind":"art","reference":"https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?search=Dance%20at%20Le%20Moulin%20de%20la%20Galette","aliases":["Dance at Le Moulin de la Galette"],"photos":[{"src":"/.netlify/functions/access?action=media&name=4e73c7f3dbf7da834d0436b8.webp","credit":"Pierre-Auguste Renoir","license":"Public domain","sourceUrl":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Renoir,_Pierre-Auguste_-_Dance_at_Le_Moulin_de_la_Galette,_1876.jpg","caption":"Identified work. Sculpture photographs may show later casts or surviving copies. Shown: Bal du moulin de la Galette · 1876"},{"src":"/.netlify/functions/access?action=media&name=4e73c7f3dbf7da834d0436b8.webp","credit":"Pierre-Auguste Renoir","license":"Public domain","sourceUrl":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Renoir,_Pierre-Auguste_-_Dance_at_Le_Moulin_de_la_Galette,_1876.jpg","licenseUrl":""}],"questionIds":["GEN43-Q01240","PDF33-Q080-A"],"tapestryIds":["t68-f6225ff0139e"],"museumIds":[],"mapIds":[],"note":"A scene of Parisian leisure joining crowded figures and shifting outdoor light.","creator":"Pierre-Auguste Renoir","assetIds":["T81-t68-f6225ff0139e"]},{"id":"LE102-21200e50d87deb6d","title":"Constantin Brâncuși","kind":"person","reference":"https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?search=Constantin%20Br%C3%A2ncu%C8%99i","aliases":["Constantin Brâncuși"],"photos":[],"questionIds":[],"tapestryIds":["t68-2a176a57f8f2"],"museumIds":[],"mapIds":[],"note":"Romanian-born sculptor working in Paris; simplified forms explore essences rather than literal likeness."},{"id":"LE102-1a0553c0e2249465","title":"Congress of Berlin","kind":"history","reference":"https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?search=Congress%20of%20Berlin","aliases":["Congress of Berlin"],"photos":[],"questionIds":["GEN43-Q03816","ARCHED-NEW101-0497"],"tapestryIds":["t68-9bd515fd02b9"],"museumIds":[],"mapIds":[],"note":"Revised the Treaty of San Stefano and rearranged Balkan territories and sovereignty."},{"id":"LE102-6d90769954aafe94","title":"Human, All Too Human","kind":"person","reference":"https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?search=Human%2C%20All%20Too%20Human","aliases":["Human, All Too Human"],"photos":[],"questionIds":[],"tapestryIds":["t68-d21226673cee"],"museumIds":[],"mapIds":[],"note":"A philosophical work marking a change in Nietzsche's thinking.","creator":"Friedrich Nietzsche"},{"id":"LE102-9effff24702209d0","title":"Edison's practical incandescent lamp demonstrations","kind":"history","reference":"https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?search=Edison%27s%20practical%20incandescent%20lamp%20demonstrations","aliases":["Edison's practical incandescent lamp demonstrations"],"photos":[],"questionIds":[],"tapestryIds":["t68-5cd4e0771ac0"],"museumIds":[],"mapIds":[],"note":"Commercial electric lighting followed many earlier experiments; avoid attributing the entire invention to one person."},{"id":"LE102-665ebdc61675e4fa","title":"Kazimir Malevich","kind":"person","reference":"https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?search=Kazimir%20Malevich","aliases":["Kazimir Malevich"],"photos":[],"questionIds":["PDF33-Q098-B"],"tapestryIds":["t68-e6dc8c9d8e90"],"museumIds":[],"mapIds":[],"note":"Founder of Suprematism; black and white squares have distinct dates and versions."},{"id":"LE102-6253cbeddd88cf68","title":"Paul Klee","kind":"person","reference":"https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?search=Paul%20Klee","aliases":["Paul Klee"],"photos":[],"questionIds":[],"tapestryIds":["t68-564f8224b5b5"],"museumIds":[],"mapIds":[],"note":"Swiss-born artist and Bauhaus teacher; personal symbolism and colour theory shaped his work."},{"id":"LE102-cdcb51461f3be6ce","title":"The Brothers Karamazov","kind":"person","reference":"https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?search=The%20Brothers%20Karamazov","aliases":["The Brothers Karamazov"],"photos":[],"questionIds":[],"tapestryIds":["t68-4be1d59a0546"],"museumIds":[],"mapIds":[],"note":"A philosophical family novel; compare ethical questions with Crime and Punishment.","creator":"Fyodor Dostoevsky"},{"id":"LE102-5dac0fa23309b48d","title":"The Thinker","kind":"art","reference":"https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?search=The%20Thinker","aliases":["The Thinker"],"photos":[{"src":"/.netlify/functions/access?action=media&name=31edc6542179030c4e68a6de.webp","credit":"Kaisching","license":"Public domain","sourceUrl":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Le_Penseur_by_Rodin_%28Kunsthalle_Bielefeld%29_2014-04-10.JPG","caption":"Identified work. Sculpture photographs may show later casts or surviving copies."},{"src":"/.netlify/functions/access?action=media&name=31edc6542179030c4e68a6de.webp","credit":"Kaisching","license":"Public domain","sourceUrl":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Le_Penseur_by_Rodin_%28Kunsthalle_Bielefeld%29_2014-04-10.JPG","licenseUrl":""},{"src":"/.netlify/functions/access?action=media&name=31edc6542179030c4e68a6de.webp","credit":"Kaisching","license":"Public domain","sourceUrl":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Le_Penseur_by_Rodin_%28Kunsthalle_Bielefeld%29_2014-04-10.JPG","licenseUrl":""}],"questionIds":["GEN43-Q01241","GEN43-Q03726","ALPHA-B011-Q945"],"tapestryIds":["t68-b7e0d1b9bcca"],"museumIds":["ART93-t68-b7e0d1b9bcca"],"mapIds":[],"note":"Conceived for The Gates of Hell; enlarged versions and bronze casts have later dates.","creator":"Auguste Rodin","assetIds":["ART93-t68-b7e0d1b9bcca","REV84-IMAGE-1241","REV84-IMAGE-3726"]},{"id":"LE102-a537cf00fd645f5a","title":"Isle of the Dead: versions","kind":"art","reference":"https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?search=Isle%20of%20the%20Dead%3A%20versions","aliases":["Isle of the Dead: versions"],"photos":[{"src":"/.netlify/functions/access?action=media&name=9b089840f1f1c3996e9f1253.webp","credit":"Arnold Böcklin","license":"Public domain","sourceUrl":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Arnold_B%C3%B6cklin_-_Die_Toteninsel_I_%28Basel%2C_Kunstmuseum%29.jpg","caption":"Representative work from the series/cycle; the timeline range covers the series, not only this image."}],"questionIds":[],"tapestryIds":["t68-084aa1c97ee0"],"museumIds":[],"mapIds":[],"note":"Böcklin painted five versions; the photo does not identify which one, so no single version is assumed.","creator":"Arnold Böcklin"},{"id":"LE102-2f526086036868da","title":"Divisionism and optical colour mixing","kind":"art","reference":"https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?search=Divisionism%20and%20optical%20colour%20mixing","aliases":["Divisionism and optical colour mixing"],"photos":[],"questionIds":[],"tapestryIds":["t69-dd3d0346fbda"],"museumIds":[],"mapIds":[],"note":"Separate strokes or dots of colour are placed beside one another. Divisionism concerns colour separation; Pointillism refers more specifically to a dotted application."},{"id":"LE102-1f68d52dda3bdcb0","title":"Symbolism and subjective meaning","kind":"art","reference":"https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?search=Symbolism%20and%20subjective%20meaning","aliases":["Symbolism and subjective meaning"],"photos":[],"questionIds":[],"tapestryIds":["t69-dd3ff48ec544"],"museumIds":[],"mapIds":[],"note":"Dream, myth and suggestion can take priority over everyday observation. Symbolism connects literature and visual art without prescribing one technique."},{"id":"LE102-d5a233bcf67ef260","title":"French protectorate established in Tunisia","kind":"history","reference":"https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?search=French%20protectorate%20established%20in%20Tunisia","aliases":["French protectorate established in Tunisia"],"photos":[],"questionIds":["ARCHED-NEW101-0487"],"tapestryIds":["t68-3d04f6a1be56"],"museumIds":[],"mapIds":[],"note":"French colonial expansion intensified rivalry with Italy in the Mediterranean."},{"id":"LE102-0f83e6a3c16e3244","title":"Pablo Picasso","kind":"person","reference":"https://www.moma.org/artists/4609","aliases":["Pablo Picasso"],"photos":[],"questionIds":["PDF33-Q093-B","PDF34-Q-096-B"],"tapestryIds":["t68-a08af765017e"],"museumIds":[],"mapIds":[],"note":"Spanish artist active in France; his work spans multiple movements and political contexts."},{"id":"LE102-6b5244f46629f5eb","title":"British occupation of Egypt","kind":"history","reference":"https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?search=British%20occupation%20of%20Egypt","aliases":["British occupation of Egypt"],"photos":[],"questionIds":["ARCHED-NEW101-0504"],"tapestryIds":["t68-d6c5233e65a5"],"museumIds":[],"mapIds":[],"note":"Occupation followed military intervention; Egypt's formal status did not simply become a British colony in 1882."},{"id":"LE102-873fc23e57b11e25","title":"Execution of Guglielmo Oberdan","kind":"history","reference":"https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?search=Execution%20of%20Guglielmo%20Oberdan","aliases":["Execution of Guglielmo Oberdan"],"photos":[],"questionIds":[],"tapestryIds":["t68-8a8d867044dd"],"museumIds":[],"mapIds":[],"note":"An Italian irredentist executed by Austria; the episode became a symbol in nationalist memory."},{"id":"LE102-6c56707d0c1f7039","title":"Triple Alliance formed","kind":"history","reference":"https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?search=Triple%20Alliance%20formed","aliases":["Triple Alliance formed"],"photos":[],"questionIds":["ARCHED-NEW101-0485"],"tapestryIds":["t68-0ba6575cd3b4"],"museumIds":[],"mapIds":[],"note":"Germany, Austria-Hungary and Italy formed an alliance; Italy later entered World War I on the opposing side."},{"id":"LE102-f92e2525ccdea7c1","title":"Umberto Boccioni","kind":"person","reference":"https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?search=Umberto%20Boccioni","aliases":["Umberto Boccioni"],"photos":[],"questionIds":["ALPHA-B003-Q200","PDF33-Q095-B","PDF35-CON-029-A"],"tapestryIds":["t68-9b6c228873f3"],"museumIds":[],"mapIds":[],"note":"Futurist painter and sculptor exploring dynamic movement."},{"id":"LE102-f7d2579334161150","title":"Georges Braque","kind":"person","reference":"https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?search=Georges%20Braque","aliases":["Georges Braque"],"photos":[],"questionIds":["PDF34-Q-103-B"],"tapestryIds":["t68-d09648b35180"],"museumIds":[],"mapIds":[],"note":"With Picasso, developed Cubism; later work continued beyond its early phases."},{"id":"LE102-86066307a78993a5","title":"Koch's cholera investigations","kind":"history","reference":"https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?search=Koch%27s%20cholera%20investigations","aliases":["Koch's cholera investigations"],"photos":[],"questionIds":[],"tapestryIds":["t68-081dddd265b4"],"museumIds":[],"mapIds":[],"note":"Koch identified the cholera bacillus during work in Egypt and India; Pacini had described the organism in 1854."},{"id":"LE102-9fd1e14919b83731","title":"Walter Gropius","kind":"person","reference":"https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?search=Walter%20Gropius","aliases":["Walter Gropius"],"photos":[],"questionIds":["GEN43-Q03692","ARCHED-NEW99-0738","ARCHED-NEW101-0244","ARCHED-NEW101-0245","ALPHA-B007-Q572","PDF-HA-BAUHAUS-WEIMAR","PDF33-Q114-B","PDF34-Q-159-B","PDF35-Q069-B","PDF35-Q079-B"],"tapestryIds":["t68-07c6780ca9da"],"museumIds":[],"mapIds":[],"note":"Founder of Bauhaus; later taught and practised in the United States."},{"id":"LE102-060cc5a558df8b12","title":"Berlin Conference on Africa","kind":"history","reference":"https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?search=Berlin%20Conference%20on%20Africa","aliases":["Berlin Conference on Africa"],"photos":[],"questionIds":[],"tapestryIds":["t68-cd925aef144f"],"museumIds":[],"mapIds":[],"note":"European powers negotiated rules for colonial claims; African peoples were not represented."},{"id":"LE102-07964641bc284267","title":"Home Insurance Building","kind":"architecture","reference":"https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?search=Home%20Insurance%20Building","aliases":["Home Insurance Building"],"photos":[{"src":"/.netlify/functions/access?action=media&name=0d178f654bc89b0f29d88e7e.webp","sourceUrl":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Home_Insurance_Building.JPG","credit":"Chicago Architectural Photographing Company","license":"Public domain","licenseUrl":null,"width":660,"height":880,"file":"Home_Insurance_Building.JPG"}],"questionIds":["PDF35-Q067-A","PDF35-CON-005-A"],"tapestryIds":["t68-3033047cde4b"],"museumIds":[],"mapIds":[],"note":"An early Chicago tall-building experiment; the label first skyscraper depends on structural definitions.","built":"1884","creator":"William Le Baron Jenney","lat":41.8796,"lon":-87.632,"coordinateSource":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Home_Insurance_Building","resolvedTitle102":"Home Insurance Building","placeId":"LE102-07964641bc284267"},{"id":"LE102-a97d3c574b6e75ad","title":"A Sunday on La Grande Jatte","kind":"art","reference":"https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?search=A%20Sunday%20on%20La%20Grande%20Jatte","aliases":["A Sunday on La Grande Jatte"],"photos":[{"src":"/.netlify/functions/access?action=media&name=655f387484a9096b22ea6167.webp","credit":"Georges Seurat · Wikimedia Commons","license":"Rights at source · Commons reference","sourceUrl":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:A_Sunday_on_La_Grande_Jatte%2C_Georges_Seurat%2C_1884.jpg","caption":"Identified work. Sculpture photographs may show later casts or surviving copies. Shown: A Sunday Afternoon on the Island of La Grande Jatte · 1886"}],"questionIds":["ARCHED-B100-20261007-023"],"tapestryIds":["t68-494084f25637"],"museumIds":[],"mapIds":[],"note":"Systematic dots of colour and a highly organised composition distinguish Neo-Impressionism from a purely spontaneous sketch.","creator":"Georges Seurat"},{"id":"LE102-105580e9784a7714","title":"The Burghers of Calais","kind":"art","reference":"https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?search=The%20Burghers%20of%20Calais","aliases":["The Burghers of Calais"],"photos":[{"src":"/.netlify/functions/access?action=media&name=f8792c53f0bc455840c0dc3d.webp","credit":"Romainberth","license":"CC BY-SA 3.0","sourceUrl":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Statue_bourgeois_calais_rodin.jpg","caption":"Identified work. Sculpture photographs may show later casts or surviving copies."}],"questionIds":[],"tape