ressionism","aliases":["Post-Impressionism"],"photos":[],"questionIds":[],"tapestryIds":["t68-6af11401a6c0"],"museumIds":[],"mapIds":[],"note":"A retrospective umbrella term for diverse approaches, not a unified group with one manifesto.","creator":"Paul Cézanne, Vincent van Gogh, Paul Gauguin, Georges Seurat"},{"id":"LE102-f732ddecfa55ce96","title":"Ludwig Mies van der Rohe","kind":"person","reference":"https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?search=Ludwig%20Mies%20van%20der%20Rohe","aliases":["Ludwig Mies van der Rohe"],"photos":[],"questionIds":["ARCHED-NEW101-0246","ARCHED-NEW101-0249","ARCHED-NEW101-0250","ARCHED-NEW101-0251","PDF34-Q-163-B"],"tapestryIds":["t68-952bd50f99e7"],"museumIds":[],"mapIds":[],"note":"Modernist architect and final Bauhaus director, later based in Chicago."},{"id":"LE102-d3dcbabd468ac709","title":"Le Corbusier","kind":"person","reference":"https://www.moma.org/artists/3426","aliases":["Le Corbusier"],"photos":[],"questionIds":["GEN43-Q03680","GEN43-Q03681","GEN43-Q04329","GEN43-Q04339","ARCHED-NEW99-0004","ARCHED-NEW99-0093","ARCHED-NEW101-0245","ARCHED-NEW101-0246","ARCHED-NEW101-0249","ARCHED-NEW101-0250","ALPHA-B001-Q038","ALPHA-B002-Q129","ALPHA-B009-Q788","ALPHA-B010-Q900","PDF34-Q-152-B","PDF34-Q-153-B","PDF34-CON-032-A","PDF34-CON-033-A"],"tapestryIds":["t68-569804451228"],"museumIds":[],"mapIds":[],"note":"Swiss-born architect and urban theorist; modernist villas and later sculptural buildings differ markedly."},{"id":"LE102-b4889610bc5bd7ea","title":"Marc Chagall","kind":"person","reference":"https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?search=Marc%20Chagall","aliases":["Marc Chagall"],"photos":[],"questionIds":["PDF34-Q-093-B","PDF34-CON-021-A"],"tapestryIds":["t68-1e368bbdf119"],"museumIds":[],"mapIds":[],"note":"Artist combining personal memory, Jewish culture and imaginative figures."},{"id":"LE102-95cf5866a485e01c","title":"Isle of Life","kind":"art","reference":"https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?search=Isle%20of%20Life","aliases":["Isle of Life"],"photos":[{"src":"/.netlify/functions/access?action=media&name=fe42bb5dbf2438f3ed072916.webp","credit":"Arnold Böcklin","license":"Public domain","sourceUrl":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:B%C3%B6cklin_-_Die_Lebensinsel_-1888.jpeg","caption":"Identified work. Sculpture photographs may show later casts or surviving copies."}],"questionIds":[],"tapestryIds":["t68-1702a47de669"],"museumIds":[],"mapIds":[],"note":"A counterpart in mood to the Isle of the Dead; compare colour, movement and symbolism.","creator":"Arnold Böcklin"},{"id":"LE102-17790200cdf669b7","title":"Giorgio de Chirico","kind":"person","reference":"https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?search=Giorgio%20de%20Chirico","aliases":["Giorgio de Chirico"],"photos":[],"questionIds":["ALPHA-B002-Q114","PDF33-Q099-B"],"tapestryIds":["t68-f361adb5bfb9"],"museumIds":[],"mapIds":[],"note":"Metaphysical painting uses enigmatic plazas, shadows and unexpected juxtapositions."},{"id":"LE102-b4e76184b989788c","title":"Brazil becomes a republic","kind":"history","reference":"https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?search=Brazil%20becomes%20a%20republic","aliases":["Brazil becomes a republic"],"photos":[],"questionIds":["ARCHED-NEW101-0462"],"tapestryIds":["t68-e9a5b6eba7dd"],"museumIds":[],"mapIds":[],"note":"A military coup ended the Brazilian Empire."},{"id":"LE102-585c17548d8e3649","title":"Eiffel Tower opens","kind":"history","reference":"https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?search=Eiffel%20Tower%20opens","aliases":["Eiffel Tower opens"],"photos":[],"questionIds":[],"tapestryIds":["t68-bc07b7681c60"],"museumIds":[],"mapIds":[],"note":"Built for the Paris Exposition Universelle; industrial engineering became a monumental urban landmark."},{"id":"LE102-8b4dc949fa50122a","title":"The Twilight of the Idols","kind":"person","reference":"https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?search=The%20Twilight%20of%20the%20Idols","aliases":["The Twilight of the Idols"],"photos":[],"questionIds":[],"tapestryIds":["t68-95691e4278ff"],"museumIds":[],"mapIds":[],"note":"Written in 1888 and published in 1889; distinguish composition from publication.","creator":"Friedrich Nietzsche"},{"id":"LE102-598a9bf33378e35f","title":"Wheatfield with Crows","kind":"art","reference":"https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?search=Wheatfield%20with%20Crows","aliases":["Wheatfield with Crows"],"photos":[{"src":"/.netlify/functions/access?action=media&name=d5c48a2b7e9b944b03e04af8.webp","credit":"Vincent van Gogh","license":"Public domain","sourceUrl":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Wheatfield_with_Crows","caption":"Exact title and artist matched to existing catalogue"},{"src":"/.netlify/functions/access?action=media&name=3604789e312afbcea0764359.webp","credit":"Vincent van Gogh","license":"Public domain","sourceUrl":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Korenveld_met_kraaien_-_s0149V1962_-_Van_Gogh_Museum.jpg","licenseUrl":""},{"src":"/.netlify/functions/access?action=media&name=d5c48a2b7e9b944b03e04af8.webp","credit":"Vincent van Gogh","license":"Public domain","sourceUrl":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Wheatfield_with_Crows","licenseUrl":""},{"src":"/.netlify/functions/access?action=media&name=d5c48a2b7e9b944b03e04af8.webp","credit":"Vincent van Gogh","license":"Public domain","sourceUrl":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Wheatfield_with_Crows","licenseUrl":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/Commons:Public_domain"}],"questionIds":["GEN43-Q01245","GEN43-Q02289","ARCHED-B03-20261007-286","ADD45-Q11496"],"tapestryIds":["t68-bb64e03be9c8"],"museumIds":["PDFART48-182"],"mapIds":[],"note":"Painted at Auvers; it is not securely established as his final painting.","creator":"Vincent van Gogh","assetIds":["PDFART48-182","T81-t68-bb64e03be9c8","HANDOFF95-IMAGE-d5c48a2b7e9b944b03e0"],"placeId":"MAP103-Q224124"},{"id":"LE102-7828c16c149f2a0a","title":"Wounded Knee massacre","kind":"history","reference":"https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?search=Wounded%20Knee%20massacre","aliases":["Wounded Knee massacre"],"photos":[],"questionIds":[],"tapestryIds":["t68-1e2956f97fc9"],"museumIds":[],"mapIds":[],"note":"US troops killed Lakota people; retain the specific event rather than presenting indigenous resistance as simply ending."},{"id":"LE102-d8a2e1b0fa321417","title":"Wainwright Building","kind":"architecture","reference":"https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?search=Wainwright%20Building","aliases":["Wainwright Building"],"photos":[{"src":"/.netlify/functions/access?action=media&name=80841b782858da5c0fc636d3.webp","sourceUrl":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Wainwright_Building,_7th_Street_and_Chestnut_Street,_St._Louis,_MO_-_53051647915.jpg","credit":"w_lemay","license":"CC BY-SA 2.0","licenseUrl":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/2.0","width":825,"height":1100,"file":"Wainwright_Building,_7th_Street_and_Chestnut_Street,_St._Louis,_MO_-_53051647915.jpg"}],"questionIds":["GEN43-Q01246"],"tapestryIds":["t68-9d95045cb17c"],"museumIds":[],"mapIds":[],"note":"A steel-framed office building whose composition articulates tall-building function.","built":"1890","creator":"Louis Sullivan, Dankmar Adler","resolvedTitle102":"Wainwright Building"},{"id":"LE102-3772450d557cacdd","title":"Mont Sainte-Victoire: series","kind":"art","reference":"https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?search=Mont%20Sainte-Victoire%3A%20series","aliases":["Mont Sainte-Victoire: series"],"photos":[{"src":"/.netlify/functions/access?action=media&name=c2b58b0fd765a4a1eb0cfee7.webp","credit":"Paul Cézanne","license":"Public domain","sourceUrl":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Paul_C%C3%A9zanne_-_Montagne_Saint-victoire_-_Google_Art_Project.jpg","caption":"Representative work from the series/cycle; the timeline range covers the series, not only this image."},{"src":"/.netlify/functions/access?action=media&name=c2b58b0fd765a4a1eb0cfee7.webp","credit":"Paul Cézanne","license":"Public domain","sourceUrl":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Paul_C%C3%A9zanne_-_Montagne_Saint-victoire_-_Google_Art_Project.jpg","licenseUrl":""}],"questionIds":["GEN43-Q04362"],"tapestryIds":["t68-ca0cc3d6be06"],"museumIds":[],"mapIds":[],"note":"Cézanne returned to this subject across many years; the range is a study window, not the date of every version.","creator":"Paul Cézanne","assetIds":["REV85-IMAGE-4362"]},{"id":"LE102-f7dcb44bf64cce9e","title":"The Card Players: series","kind":"art","reference":"https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?search=The%20Card%20Players%3A%20series","aliases":["The Card Players: series"],"photos":[{"src":"/.netlify/functions/access?action=media&name=c0c9bd517d30a5f1ad317da7.webp","credit":"Paul Cézanne","license":"Public domain","sourceUrl":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Les_Joueurs_de_cartes%2C_par_Paul_C%C3%A9zanne.jpg","caption":"One version of Cézanne's Card Players series. The timeline spans the series; the photographed canvas is identified in the image source."}],"questionIds":[],"tapestryIds":["t68-75f46fc7fd5f"],"museumIds":[],"mapIds":[],"note":"A series generally dated to the early 1890s; the photo does not securely identify one version.","creator":"Paul Cézanne"},{"id":"LE102-c1faca0af536d4cc","title":"Art Nouveau","kind":"history","reference":"https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?search=Art%20Nouveau","aliases":["Art Nouveau"],"photos":[],"questionIds":["ALPHA-B004-Q322","ALPHA-B006-Q638","ALPHA-B007-Q561","ALPHA-B010-Q896","ALPHA-B010-Q906","ALPHA-B010-Q907","ALPHA-B010-Q936","PDF-HA-GUIMARD-METRO"],"tapestryIds":["t68-4995b1958c6a"],"museumIds":[],"mapIds":[],"note":"Approximate international movement joining architecture and decorative arts; local names and forms differ.","built":"1890","resolvedTitle102":null},{"id":"LE102-f96c758f9effed61","title":"Art Nouveau, Liberty and Jugendstil","kind":"architecture","reference":"https://www.vam.ac.uk/articles/art-nouveau-an-international-style","aliases":["Art Nouveau, Liberty and Jugendstil"],"photos":[],"questionIds":[],"tapestryIds":["t69-0b060caf201a"],"museumIds":[],"mapIds":[],"note":"Related international movements used regionally different names and forms. Italian Liberty and German Jugendstil belong to this context; Art Deco is a later, distinct label.","built":"1890"},{"id":"LE102-0e994e0d7905caa5","title":"Gesamtkunstwerk and the designed interior","kind":"architecture","reference":"https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?search=Gesamtkunstwerk%20and%20the%20designed%20interior","aliases":["Gesamtkunstwerk and the designed interior"],"photos":[],"questionIds":[],"tapestryIds":["t69-e3c500479154"],"museumIds":[],"mapIds":[],"note":"The idea of a total work of art coordinates architecture, furnishings and other arts. It is not confined to a single movement or designer.","built":"1890"},{"id":"LE102-bd1e3d200a6a0eb2","title":"Naum Gabo","kind":"person","reference":"https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?search=Naum%20Gabo","aliases":["Naum Gabo"],"photos":[],"questionIds":[],"tapestryIds":["t68-5bb2363ee7e4"],"museumIds":[],"mapIds":[],"note":"Constructivist sculptor investigating space, transparency and movement."},{"id":"LE102-70e168f66f9191a1","title":"Max Ernst","kind":"person","reference":"https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?search=Max%20Ernst","aliases":["Max Ernst"],"photos":[],"questionIds":[],"tapestryIds":["t68-c23f64d9e374"],"museumIds":[],"mapIds":[],"note":"Dada and Surrealist artist employing collage and experimental techniques."},{"id":"LE102-81b71bd478d7820e","title":"Rouen Cathedral: series","kind":"art","reference":"https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?search=Rouen%20Cathedral%3A%20series","aliases":["Rouen Cathedral: series"],"photos":[{"src":"/.netlify/functions/access?action=media&name=309bb221c9e9fc1947ec8b8e.webp","credit":"Claude Monet","license":"Public domain","sourceUrl":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:RouenCathedral_Monet_1894.jpg","caption":"Representative work from the series/cycle; the timeline range covers the series, not only this image. Shown: Rouen Cathedral in Full Sunlight · 1892–1893"}],"questionIds":["PDF33-Q079-A"],"tapestryIds":["t68-6171d8820364"],"museumIds":[],"mapIds":[],"note":"Serial painting compares changing light on one architectural motif; production and exhibition dates differ.","creator":"Claude Monet"},{"id":"LE102-ea181a612fb56485","title":"At the Moulin Rouge","kind":"art","reference":"https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?search=At%20the%20Moulin%20Rouge","aliases":["At the Moulin Rouge"],"photos":[{"src":"/.netlify/functions/access?action=media&name=6511ce3d91fdc21653a19e03.webp","credit":"Henri de Toulouse-Lautrec","license":"Public domain","sourceUrl":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Henri_de_Toulouse-Lautrec%2C_At_the_Moulin_Rouge.jpg","caption":"Identified work. Sculpture photographs may show later casts or surviving copies."}],"questionIds":[],"tapestryIds":["t68-275c6dbd6a63"],"museumIds":[],"mapIds":[],"note":"A modern nightlife scene with radical cropping and unnatural lighting; commonly dated approximately 1892–1895.","creator":"Henri de Toulouse-Lautrec"},{"id":"LE102-e51050fdf372f299","title":"New Zealand grants women parliamentary voting rights","kind":"history","reference":"https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?search=New%20Zealand%20grants%20women%20parliamentary%20voting%20rights","aliases":["New Zealand grants women parliamentary voting rights"],"photos":[],"questionIds":["ARCHED-NEW101-0518"],"tapestryIds":["t68-df76ee732010"],"museumIds":[],"mapIds":[],"note":"A landmark in national suffrage; eligibility and participation still depended on other legal conditions."},{"id":"LE102-faf7367916a64a30","title":"The Scream","kind":"art","reference":"https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?search=The%20Scream","aliases":["The Scream"],"photos":[{"src":"/.netlify/functions/access?action=media&name=303bfcb847f3ceb56b920f06.webp","credit":"Edvard Munch","license":"Public domain","sourceUrl":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Edvard_Munch%2C_1893%2C_The_Scream%2C_oil%2C_tempera_and_pastel_on_cardboard%2C_91_x_73_cm%2C_National_Gallery_of_Norway.jpg","caption":"Identified work. Sculpture photographs may show later casts or surviving copies."},{"src":"/.netlify/functions/access?action=media&name=303bfcb847f3ceb56b920f06.webp","credit":"Edvard Munch","license":"Public domain","sourceUrl":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Edvard_Munch%2C_1893%2C_The_Scream%2C_oil%2C_tempera_and_pastel_on_cardboard%2C_91_x_73_cm%2C_National_Gallery_of_Norway.jpg","licenseUrl":""}],"questionIds":["ARCHED-B100-20261007-027","ALPHA-B003-Q191","PDF33-Q091-A"],"tapestryIds":["t68-1c449f97fb23"],"museumIds":["ART93-t68-1c449f97fb23"],"mapIds":[],"note":"Several painted and printed versions exist; 1893 refers to the early painted version.","creator":"Edvard Munch","assetIds":["ART93-t68-1c449f97fb23"]},{"id":"LE102-0df28cef9dd97f5e","title":"Dreyfus affair begins","kind":"history","reference":"https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?search=Dreyfus%20affair%20begins","aliases":["Dreyfus affair begins"],"photos":[],"questionIds":[],"tapestryIds":["t68-7754f17e77c9"],"museumIds":[],"mapIds":[],"note":"A wrongful treason conviction exposed antisemitism and divided French society; Zola intervened in 1898."},{"id":"LE102-8da75545d1d39c4c","title":"Marconi's early radio experiments","kind":"history","reference":"https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?search=Marconi%27s%20early%20radio%20experiments","aliases":["Marconi's early radio experiments"],"photos":[],"questionIds":[],"tapestryIds":["t68-e35d5bc71db8"],"museumIds":[],"mapIds":[],"note":"Wireless communication developed through several researchers; distinguish experiments from later commercial transmission."},{"id":"LE102-24c4e681b1166082","title":"Röntgen discovers X-rays","kind":"history","reference":"https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?search=R%C3%B6ntgen%20discovers%20X-rays","aliases":["Röntgen discovers X-rays"],"photos":[],"questionIds":["ARCHED-NEW101-0528","ARCHED-NEW101-0529","ARCHED-NEW101-0532"],"tapestryIds":["t68-e1af717c8e67"],"museumIds":[],"mapIds":[],"note":"A major transformation in medical imaging and physical science."},{"id":"LE102-1bd47e8c68558af4","title":"First modern Olympic Games in Athens","kind":"history","reference":"https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?search=First%20modern%20Olympic%20Games%20in%20Athens","aliases":["First modern Olympic Games in Athens"],"photos":[],"questionIds":["ARCHED-NEW101-0512"],"tapestryIds":["t68-f333d3951437"],"museumIds":[],"mapIds":[],"note":"The revived international Games drew on an idealised classical heritage."},{"id":"LE102-c1097488b305b43c","title":"Where Do We Come From? What Are We? Where Are We Going?","kind":"art","reference":"https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?search=Where%20Do%20We%20Come%20From%3F%20What%20Are%20We%3F%20Where%20Are%20We%20Going%3F","aliases":["Where Do We Come From? What Are We? Where Are We Going?"],"photos":[{"src":"/.netlify/functions/access?action=media&name=381b37eaa8802529aa007de7.webp","credit":"Paul Gauguin","license":"Public domain","sourceUrl":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Gauguin_-_Where_Do_We_Come_From%3F_What_Are_We%3F_Where_Are_We_Going%3F_%281897-98%29.jpg","caption":"Identified work. Sculpture photographs may show later casts or surviving copies."},{"src":"/.netlify/functions/access?action=media&name=381b37eaa8802529aa007de7.webp","credit":"Paul Gauguin","license":"Public domain","sourceUrl":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Gauguin_-_Where_Do_We_Come_From%3F_What_Are_We%3F_Where_Are_We_Going%3F_%281897-98%29.jpg","licenseUrl":""}],"questionIds":["GEN43-Q01247"],"tapestryIds":["t68-80268f20f603"],"museumIds":[],"mapIds":[],"note":"Painted in Tahiti in 1897–1898; a symbolic work shaped by colonial-era encounters and the artist's inventions.","creator":"Paul Gauguin","assetIds":["T81-t68-80268f20f603"]},{"id":"LE102-740747244b468d99","title":"Vienna Secession and artistic independence","kind":"art","reference":"https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?search=Vienna%20Secession%20and%20artistic%20independence","aliases":["Vienna Secession and artistic independence"],"photos":[],"questionIds":[],"tapestryIds":["t69-d04bdbaf24ce"],"museumIds":[],"mapIds":[],"note":"The Secession challenged established exhibition structures and embraced multiple artistic approaches. Klimt, Olbrich and Hoffmann worked in different media."},{"id":"LE102-f5cf67ef3af0478f","title":"Water Lilies: series","kind":"art","reference":"https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?search=Water%20Lilies%3A%20series","aliases":["Water Lilies: series"],"photos":[{"src":"/.netlify/functions/access?action=media&name=53013d234e0fc4b7976cc101.webp","credit":"Claude Monet","license":"Image © respective rights holders · MoMA collection","sourceUrl":"https://www.moma.org/collection/works/80220","caption":"Representative work from the series/cycle; the timeline range covers the series, not only this image. Shown: Water Lilies · 1914-26"}],"questionIds":[],"tapestryIds":["t68-c967e980955a"],"museumIds":[],"mapIds":[],"note":"A long-running Giverny subject culminating in immersive late panels; no single canvas is implied.","creator":"Claude Monet"},{"id":"LE102-82c706b06f39d2ad","title":"Paul Delvaux","kind":"person","reference":"https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?search=Paul%20Delvaux","aliases":["Paul Delvaux"],"photos":[],"questionIds":[],"tapestryIds":["t68-e81d4c5a0657"],"museumIds":[],"mapIds":[],"note":"Belgian painter of enigmatic figures, architecture and nocturnal settings."},{"id":"LE102-8271296e8d426f86","title":"Curie research identifies polonium and radium","kind":"history","reference":"https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?search=Curie%20research%20identifies%20polonium%20and%20radium","aliases":["Curie research identifies polonium and radium"],"photos":[],"questionIds":[],"tapestryIds":["t68-f09297ff6c7f"],"museumIds":[],"mapIds":[],"note":"Marie and Pierre Curie's investigations advanced the study of radioactivity."},{"id":"LE102-a21e192b853038af","title":"Fashoda Incident","kind":"history","reference":"https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?search=Fashoda%20Incident","aliases":["Fashoda Incident"],"photos":[],"questionIds":["ARCHED-NEW101-0126","ARCHED-NEW101-0530"],"tapestryIds":["t68-46522f29972d"],"museumIds":[],"mapIds":[],"note":"A colonial confrontation in Sudan; later Anglo-French rapprochement had multiple causes."},{"id":"LE102-4f6305bd7f98529f","title":"Spanish–American War","kind":"history","reference":"https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?search=Spanish%E2%80%93American%20War","aliases":["Spanish–American War"],"photos":[],"questionIds":["ARCHED-NEW101-0465"],"tapestryIds":["t68-cbc908209ff1"],"museumIds":[],"mapIds":[],"note":"Spain lost control of major overseas possessions; US imperial power expanded."},{"id":"LE102-58682073668dba22","title":"Zola publishes J'accuse","kind":"history","reference":"https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?search=Zola%20publishes%20J%27accuse","aliases":["Zola publishes J'accuse"],"photos":[],"questionIds":["ARCHED-NEW101-0475"],"tapestryIds":["t68-51939b46594c"],"museumIds":[],"mapIds":[],"note":"An open letter challenged the handling of the Dreyfus affair."},{"id":"LE102-89a910a1da641f6b","title":"The Large Bathers","kind":"art","reference":"https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?search=The%20Large%20Bathers","aliases":["The Large Bathers"],"photos":[{"src":"/.netlify/functions/access?action=media&name=3abf80a911729358c23d7263.webp","credit":"Paul Cézanne","license":"Public domain","sourceUrl":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Paul_C%C3%A9zanne%2C_French_-_The_Large_Bathers_-_Google_Art_Project.jpg","caption":"The Large Bathers, Philadelphia Museum of Art version, 1906. Full painting."}],"questionIds":[],"tapestryIds":["t68-9d1de840e736"],"museumIds":[],"mapIds":[],"note":"A late work combining figures and landscape into a constructed composition; developed over several years.","creator":"Paul Cézanne"},{"id":"LE102-442a1a717f53d657","title":"René Magritte","kind":"person","reference":"https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?search=Ren%C3%A9%20Magritte","aliases":["René Magritte"],"photos":[],"questionIds":["ALPHA-B004-Q316","PDF33-Q103-B"],"tapestryIds":["t68-14b7b273f8ba"],"museumIds":[],"mapIds":[],"note":"Belgian Surrealist examining the relationship between images, language and objects."},{"id":"LE102-ab2db69504a4dac9","title":"Alexander Calder","kind":"person","reference":"https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?search=Alexander%20Calder","aliases":["Alexander Calder"],"photos":[],"questionIds":[],"tapestryIds":["t68-0ed181d85b66"],"museumIds":[],"mapIds":[],"note":"American sculptor known for mobiles and large outdoor works."},{"id":"LE102-6d1abe458c6eb930","title":"Henry Moore","kind":"person","reference":"https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?search=Henry%20Moore","aliases":["Henry Moore"],"photos":[],"questionIds":[],"tapestryIds":["t68-f0f56df4f81b"],"museumIds":[],"mapIds":[],"note":"Sculptor of reclining figures and organic forms, often intended for outdoor settings."},{"id":"LE102-9ddc8de64369371f","title":"First Hague Peace Conference","kind":"history","reference":"https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?search=First%20Hague%20Peace%20Conference","aliases":["First Hague Peace Conference"],"photos":[],"questionIds":[],"tapestryIds":["t68-5d876b351e83"],"museumIds":[],"mapIds":[],"note":"International efforts to regulate warfare and arbitration preceded the world wars."},{"id":"LE102-bf0779d4c732a921","title":"Lucio Fontana","kind":"person","reference":"https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?search=Lucio%20Fontana","aliases":["Lucio Fontana"],"photos":[],"questionIds":["GEN43-Q04260"],"tapestryIds":["t68-ae69af07c982"],"museumIds":[],"mapIds":[],"note":"Artist associated with Spatialism; cuts and perforations turn pictorial surface into actual space."},{"id":"LE102-c47723ac4c83745c","title":"The Interpretation of Dreams","kind":"person","reference":"https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?search=The%20Interpretation%20of%20Dreams","aliases":["The Interpretation of Dreams"],"photos":[],"questionIds":[],"tapestryIds":["t68-24cfde8f07f6"],"museumIds":[],"mapIds":[],"note":"Dated 1900 on publication, though released in late 1899; the photo's 1910 marker is not its first publication.","creator":"Sigmund Freud"},{"id":"LE102-f52a469b1f16b193","title":"Expressionism and emotional distortion","kind":"art","reference":"https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?search=Expressionism%20and%20emotional%20distortion","aliases":["Expressionism and emotional distortion"],"photos":[],"questionIds":[],"tapestryIds":["t69-b313f49d3a7e"],"museumIds":[],"mapIds":[],"note":"Distorted colour, form or space can communicate psychological intensity. Expressionism is not the same movement as Abstract Expressionism after World War II."},{"id":"LE102-858aa9bf5c87c96c","title":"Totalitarianism, fascism and democracy","kind":"history","reference":"https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?search=Totalitarianism%2C%20fascism%20and%20democracy","aliases":["Totalitarianism, fascism and democracy"],"photos":[],"questionIds":[],"tapestryIds":["t69-1d353b9d3ec0"],"museumIds":[],"mapIds":[],"note":"Compare institutions, repression, propaganda and political mobilisation. Fascism and Nazism share features but have distinct histories; democratic elections alone do not secure liberal democracy."},{"id":"LE102-ff833306936f94a5","title":"Organic architecture and the site","kind":"architecture","reference":"https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?search=Organic%20architecture%20and%20the%20site","aliases":["Organic architecture and the site"],"photos":[],"questionIds":[],"tapestryIds":["t69-b0c6842a893b"],"museumIds":[],"mapIds":[],"note":"Wright sought integration of building, inhabitants, materials and landscape. Organic does not simply mean a curving shape or the use of plants.","built":"1900"},{"id":"LE102-97016d4cda10c4ad","title":"First Nobel Prizes awarded","kind":"history","reference":"https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?search=First%20Nobel%20Prizes%20awarded","aliases":["First Nobel Prizes awarded"],"photos":[],"questionIds":[],"tapestryIds":["t68-b66b9dfc527f"],"museumIds":[],"mapIds":[],"note":"The awards reflected Alfred Nobel's endowment; categories and institutions have specific histories."},{"id":"LE102-0811ea66b0d3871d","title":"Alberto Giacometti","kind":"person","reference":"https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?search=Alberto%20Giacometti","aliases":["Alberto Giacometti"],"photos":[],"questionIds":[],"tapestryIds":["t68-d532f8f5ef8d"],"museumIds":[],"mapIds":[],"note":"Swiss sculptor working in Paris; Surrealist objects preceded elongated postwar figures."},{"id":"LE102-6db45d1cab329bd2","title":"Marino Marini","kind":"person","reference":"https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?search=Marino%20Marini","aliases":["Marino Marini"],"photos":[],"questionIds":[],"tapestryIds":["t68-354646554ad2"],"museumIds":[],"mapIds":[],"note":"Italian sculptor whose recurring horse-and-rider theme changes dramatically across periods."},{"id":"LE102-0b3fceb4809e3d7a","title":"Jean Dubuffet","kind":"person","reference":"https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?search=Jean%20Dubuffet","aliases":["Jean Dubuffet"],"photos":[],"questionIds":[],"tapestryIds":["t68-d4e10d5d9422"],"museumIds":[],"mapIds":[],"note":"French artist who developed the concept of Art Brut."},{"id":"LE102-371fcd748750dc48","title":"Marcel Breuer","kind":"person","reference":"https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?search=Marcel%20Breuer","aliases":["Marcel Breuer"],"photos":[],"questionIds":[],"tapestryIds":["t68-2587c48eb87e"],"museumIds":[],"mapIds":[],"note":"Bauhaus designer and architect, known for tubular steel furniture and later concrete buildings."},{"id":"LE102-de6f6123821086b6","title":"Wright brothers' powered flight","kind":"history","reference":"https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?search=Wright%20brothers%27%20powered%20flight","aliases":["Wright brothers' powered flight"],"photos":[],"questionIds":[],"tapestryIds":["t68-5ed249a19d70"],"museumIds":[],"mapIds":[],"note":"A sustained, controlled flight at Kitty Hawk became a milestone in aviation."},{"id":"LE102-781590f0eda2fe1b","title":"Mark Rothko","kind":"person","reference":"https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?search=Mark%20Rothko","aliases":["Mark Rothko"],"photos":[],"questionIds":["PDF34-Q-108-B","PDF34-CON-022-A"],"tapestryIds":["t68-edd10ed89ace"],"museumIds":[],"mapIds":[],"note":"Painter associated with large fields of colour; distinct from Pollock's action-painting methods."},{"id":"LE102-45fe463d4cde3e79","title":"Entente Cordiale","kind":"history","reference":"https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?search=Entente%20Cordiale","aliases":["Entente Cordiale"],"photos":[],"questionIds":["GEN43-Q03819"],"tapestryIds":["t68-e1462f408752"],"museumIds":[],"mapIds":[],"note":"Agreements settled colonial disputes; they were not yet a single automatic military alliance."},{"id":"LE102-e9745cd44a676c68","title":"Russo-Japanese War","kind":"history","reference":"https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?search=Russo-Japanese%20War","aliases":["Russo-Japanese War"],"photos":[],"questionIds":[],"tapestryIds":["t68-26be6fc2928c"],"museumIds":[],"mapIds":[],"note":"Japanese victory challenged European assumptions of imperial superiority."},{"id":"LE102-7720c538f74fb782","title":"Salvador Dalí","kind":"person","reference":"https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?search=Salvador%20Dal%C3%AD","aliases":["Salvador Dalí"],"photos":[],"questionIds":["GEN43-Q04571","PDF33-Q104-B","PDF34-Q-100-B"],"tapestryIds":["t68-2bc7953405dc"],"museumIds":[],"mapIds":[],"note":"Spanish Surrealist known for precise rendering of dreamlike scenes."},{"id":"LE102-bdcf24f87772f627","title":"Bloody Sunday in Saint Petersburg","kind":"history","reference":"https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?search=Bloody%20Sunday%20in%20Saint%20Petersburg","aliases":["Bloody Sunday in Saint Petersburg"],"photos":[],"questionIds":[],"tapestryIds":["t68-bee4514d0828"],"museumIds":[],"mapIds":[],"note":"Violence against petitioners helped ignite the Russian Revolution of 1905."},{"id":"LE102-bfd3d1fc7809ddfb","title":"Einstein publishes special relativity","kind":"history","reference":"https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?search=Einstein%20publishes%20special%20relativity","aliases":["Einstein publishes special relativity"],"photos":[],"questionIds":[],"tapestryIds":["t68-48782d69bd16"],"museumIds":[],"mapIds":[],"note":"A new account of space and time; general relativity followed in 1915."},{"id":"LE102-f522db3b5c67d65d","title":"First Moroccan Crisis","kind":"history","reference":"https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?search=First%20Moroccan%20Crisis","aliases":["First Moroccan Crisis"],"photos":[],"questionIds":[],"tapestryIds":["t68-8bc3ff5e991e"],"museumIds":[],"mapIds":[],"note":"German intervention challenged French influence in Morocco and tested European diplomacy."},{"id":"LE102-ee472d45d4e7df54","title":"Industrial Workers of the World founded","kind":"history","reference":"https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?search=Industrial%20Workers%20of%20the%20World%20founded","aliases":["Industrial Workers of the World founded"],"photos":[],"questionIds":[],"tapestryIds":["t68-ad68db953ef1"],"museumIds":[],"mapIds":[],"note":"An internationalist labour organisation founded in Chicago."},{"id":"LE102-42b3747cdaacd766","title":"Woman with a Hat","kind":"art","reference":"https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?search=Woman%20with%20a%20Hat","aliases":["Woman with a Hat"],"photos":[{"src":"/.netlify/functions/access?action=media&name=1b64d606b5be1a3f9ccd74ac.webp","credit":"Henri Matisse","license":"Public domain","sourceUrl":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Matisse-Woman-with-a-Hat.jpg","caption":"Identified work. Sculpture photographs may show later casts or surviving copies."}],"questionIds":["PDF33-Q090-A"],"tapestryIds":["t68-a16a8a468cf8"],"museumIds":[],"mapIds":[],"note":"Non-naturalistic colour helped define the public reception of Fauvism.","creator":"Henri Matisse"},{"id":"LE102-6baabedac6f829d0","title":"The Joy of Life","kind":"art","reference":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Le_Bonheur_de_vivre","aliases":["The Joy of Life"],"photos":[{"src":"/.netlify/functions/access?action=media&name=0d926e59a9f99f2dd975a42b.webp","credit":"Henri Matisse","license":"Public domain","sourceUrl":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Bonheur_Matisse.jpg","caption":"Identified work. Sculpture photographs may show later casts or surviving copies."},{"src":"/.netlify/functions/access?action=media&name=0d926e59a9f99f2dd975a42b.webp","credit":"Henri Matisse","license":"Public domain","sourceUrl":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Bonheur_Matisse.jpg","licenseUrl":""}],"questionIds":["GEN43-Q01395"],"tapestryIds":["t68-635658e41984"],"museumIds":[],"mapIds":[],"note":"Also called Le Bonheur de vivre. Fauvist colour and an idealised figure landscape; the handwritten placement is not a precise creation date.","creator":"Henri Matisse","assetIds":["T81-t68-635658e41984"]},{"id":"LE102-2112b6c4d45eb2ad","title":"Fauvism","kind":"art","reference":"https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?search=Fauvism","aliases":["Fauvism"],"photos":[],"questionIds":[],"tapestryIds":["t68-7dd072993daf"],"museumIds":[],"mapIds":[],"note":"Expressive, non-naturalistic colour; dates mark a short collective moment rather than all later work by these artists.","creator":"Henri Matisse, André Derain"},{"id":"LE102-6f7d0e8d0c12dd53","title":"Fauvist colour versus naturalistic colour","kind":"art","reference":"https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?search=Fauvist%20colour%20versus%20naturalistic%20colour","aliases":["Fauvist colour versus naturalistic colour"],"photos":[],"questionIds":[],"tapestryIds":["t69-b0fa09c72c10"],"museumIds":[],"mapIds":[],"note":"Fauvist colour can be organised for expressive and compositional reasons rather than reproducing local colour. Strong colour alone does not identify a specific artist."},{"id":"LE102-e6d1346bdd69199d","title":"Seated Woman","kind":"art","reference":"https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?search=Seated%20Woman","aliases":["Seated Woman"],"photos":[{"src":"/.netlify/functions/access?action=media&name=485baaa5d9f9ac0a6899abb6.webp","credit":"Amedeo Modigliani","license":"Public domain","sourceUrl":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Amedeo_Modigliani%2C_Seated_Woman_in_a_Blue_Dress_%281917-1919%29.jpg","caption":"Contextual example: Seated Woman in a Blue Dress, 1917–1919. The handwritten generic title does not identify a unique canvas; this image is not claimed as its exact identification."}],"questionIds":[],"tapestryIds":["t68-02ede2d88618"],"museumIds":[],"mapIds":[],"note":"Unresolved title: several Modigliani portraits have this generic name. Broad working period only; no specific canvas or exact date is asserted.","creator":"Amedeo Modigliani"},{"id":"LE102-6e4c1bfb7d6c8113","title":"Les Demoiselles d'Avignon","kind":"art","reference":"https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?search=Les%20Demoiselles%20d%27Avignon","aliases":["Les Demoiselles d'Avignon"],"photos":[{"src":"/.netlify/functions/access?action=media&name=f69a37b30649d071be0d6636.webp","credit":"Image reference from Wikipedia","license":"Wikipedia non-free reference · reuse not cleared","sourceUrl":"https://www.moma.org/explore/inside_out/2010/04/14/moma-offsite-where-did-it-go/","caption":"Exact title and artist matched to existing catalogue"},{"src":"/.netlify/functions/access?action=media&name=f628b19199bd686de6ad8d64.webp","credit":"Image reference from Wikipedia","license":"Wikipedia non-free reference · reuse not cleared","sourceUrl":"https://www.moma.org/collection/works/79766","licenseUrl":""},{"src":"/.netlify/functions/access?action=media&name=f628b19199bd686de6ad8d64.webp","credit":"The Museum of Modern Art, New York · Acquired through the Lillie P. Bliss Bequest (by exchange)","license":"Image © respective rights holders · MoMA collection","sourceUrl":"https://www.moma.org/collection/works/79766","licenseUrl":"https://www.moma.org/collection/works/79766"}],"questionIds":["ADD45-Q11259","ADD45-Q11260","ADD45-Q11524","ALPHA-B003-Q175","PDF33-Q093-A"],"tapestryIds":["t68-df23c72edbcb"],"museumIds":["ART45-OFFICIAL-a3f71c927a7b","PDFART48-211"],"mapIds":[],"note":"A radical reworking of the figure and pictorial space that preceded mature Cubism.","creator":"Pablo Picasso","assetIds":["ART45-OFFICIAL-a3f71c927a7b","PDFART48-211"]},{"id":"LE102-e7fbdcdd09b8d038","title":"Triple Entente diplomatic alignment","kind":"history","reference":"https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?search=Triple%20Entente%20diplomatic%20alignment","aliases":["Triple Entente diplomatic alignment"],"photos":[],"questionIds":[],"tapestryIds":["t68-57cb0c406c3c"],"museumIds":[],"mapIds":[],"note":"The Anglo-Russian Convention completed an alignment with France; distinguish from the Triple Alliance."},{"id":"LE102-c7521887575c7890","title":"The Kiss","kind":"art","reference":"https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?search=The%20Kiss","aliases":["The Kiss"],"photos":[{"src":"/.netlify/functions/access?action=media&name=a6d3c1b825d7a0751b5ea169.webp","credit":"Gustav Klimt","license":"Public domain","sourceUrl":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:The_Kiss_-_Gustav_Klimt_-_Google_Cultural_Institute.jpg","caption":"Identified work. Sculpture photographs may show later casts or surviving copies."},{"src":"/.netlify/functions/access?action=media&name=a6d3c1b825d7a0751b5ea169.webp","credit":"Gustav Klimt","license":"Public domain","sourceUrl":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:The_Kiss_-_Gustav_Klimt_-_Google_Cultural_Institute.jpg","licenseUrl":""}],"questionIds":["GEN43-Q04516","GEN43-Q04521","ALPHA-B004-Q284","PDF33-Q072-A"],"tapestryIds":["t68-7a586eab8403"],"museumIds":[],"mapIds":[],"note":"Gold and decorative pattern envelop the embracing figures; a key work of Klimt's golden period.","creator":"Gustav Klimt","assetIds":["REV85-IMAGE-4516"]},{"id":"LE102-79399cbf7fbb164b","title":"Analytic and Synthetic Cubism","kind":"art","reference":"https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?search=Analytic%20and%20Synthetic%20Cubism","aliases":["Analytic and Synthetic Cubism"],"photos":[],"questionIds":[],"tapestryIds":["t69-01747b46cc83"],"museumIds":[],"mapIds":[],"note":"Analytic Cubism fragments and examines forms; Synthetic Cubism introduces more constructed signs, collage and broader shapes. These are phases, not two unrelated schools."},{"id":"LE102-5077d9d6eb537af7","title":"Cubism","kind":"art","reference":"https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?search=Cubism","aliases":["Cubism"],"photos":[],"questionIds":[],"tapestryIds":["t68-1b1342eae4cf"],"museumIds":[],"mapIds":[],"note":"Analytic and Synthetic phases rethought representation, viewpoint and pictorial construction.","creator":"Pablo Picasso, Georges Braque"},{"id":"LE102-c291afc139243872","title":"Austria-Hungary annexes Bosnia-Herzegovina","kind":"history","reference":"https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?search=Austria-Hungary%20annexes%20Bosnia-Herzegovina","aliases":["Austria-Hungary annexes Bosnia-Herzegovina"],"photos":[],"questionIds":[],"tapestryIds":["t68-d76b5f61a760"],"museumIds":[],"mapIds":[],"note":"Annexation intensified Balkan and great-power tensions."},{"id":"LE102-2c25b073e4c70582","title":"Harmony in Red","kind":"art","reference":"https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?search=Harmony%20in%20Red","aliases":["Harmony in Red"],"photos":[{"src":"/.netlify/functions/access?action=media&name=0624155f0369b426a47bf7f9.webp","credit":"Henri Matisse","license":"Public domain","sourceUrl":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Matisse-The-Dessert-Harmony-in-Red-Henri-1908-fast.jpg","caption":"Identified work. Sculpture photographs may show later casts or surviving copies."},{"src":"/.netlify/functions/access?action=media&name=0624155f0369b426a47bf7f9.webp","credit":"Henri Matisse","license":"Public domain","sourceUrl":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Matisse-The-Dessert-Harmony-in-Red-Henri-1908-fast.jpg","licenseUrl":""}],"questionIds":["GEN43-Q01249"],"tapestryIds":["t68-f49247b19579"],"museumIds":[],"mapIds":[],"note":"Also called The Red Room; colour and decorative pattern flatten spatial depth.","creator":"Henri Matisse","assetIds":["T81-t68-f49247b19579"]},{"id":"LE102-75bc5f3f081c3ff4","title":"Houses at L'Estaque","kind":"art","reference":"https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?search=Houses%20at%20L%27Estaque","aliases":["Houses at L'Estaque"],"photos":[{"src":"/.netlify/functions/access?action=media&name=78b94d1efbe3b9e3cd1bcdf3.webp","credit":"Georges Braque","license":"Copyrighted artwork; see source reproduction rights","sourceUrl":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:Georges_Braque,_1908,_Maisons_à_l'Estaque_(Houses_at_L'Estaque),_oil_on_canvas,_73_x_59.5_cm,_Kunst_Museum_Bern.jpg","caption":"Houses at L’Estaque, 1908, Kunstmuseum Bern. This is the Bern canvas, not the related Houses and Tree at LaM."}],"questionIds":[],"tapestryIds":["t68-87e416e34b74"],"museumIds":[],"mapIds":[],"note":"Geometric simplification of landscape is a key step towards Cubism.","creator":"Georges Braque"},{"id":"LE102-3030fd4fa56897a5","title":"Willem de Kooning","kind":"person","reference":"https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?search=Willem%20de%20Kooning","aliases":["Willem de Kooning"],"photos":[],"questionIds":[],"tapestryIds":["t68-3df53c1a3f04"],"museumIds":[],"mapIds":[],"note":"Dutch-born Abstract Expressionist active in New York; figuration and abstraction interact."},{"id":"LE102-49e219fa38030a67","title":"AEG Turbine Factory","kind":"architecture","reference":"https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?search=AEG%20Turbine%20Factory","aliases":["AEG Turbine Factory"],"photos":[{"src":"/.netlify/functions/access?action=media&name=bcad7bb57c2a2d8ca225e852.webp","sourceUrl":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Berlin_AEG_Turbinenfabrik.jpg","credit":"Doris Antony, Berlin","license":"CC BY-SA 3.0","licenseUrl":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/3.0","width":960,"height":705,"file":"Berlin_AEG_Turbinenfabrik.jpg"}],"questionIds":["ARCHED-NEW101-0244","ALPHA-B001-Q038"],"tapestryIds":["t68-58d6eed54a1d"],"museumIds":[],"mapIds":[],"note":"Industrial architecture and corporate design intersect in Berlin.","built":"1909","creator":"Peter Behrens","city":"Berlin","style":"Early modern industrial architecture","era":"Early twentieth century","resolvedTitle102":"AEG turbine factory"},{"id":"LE102-810dec15fe507783","title":"Futurist Manifesto published","kind":"art","reference":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Manifesto_of_Futurism","aliases":["Futurist Manifesto published"],"photos":[],"questionIds":[],"tapestryIds":["t68-12c8b4f5e382"],"museumIds":[],"mapIds":[],"note":"The manifesto appeared in Le Figaro; Futurist painting and architecture manifestos followed.","creator":"Filippo Tommaso Marinetti"},{"id":"LE102-c97472f6a86d112c","title":"Futurism: speed, simultaneity and modern life","kind":"art","reference":"https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?search=Futurism","aliases":["Futurism: speed, simultaneity and modern life"],"photos":[],"questionIds":[],"tapestryIds":["t69-d3188a57e846"],"museumIds":[],"mapIds":[],"note":"Futurists explored movement through repeated or interpenetrating forms. Their celebration of machines and war requires historical context, not uncritical endorsement."},{"id":"LE102-eda00df5173bf049","title":"Dance","kind":"art","reference":"https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?search=Dance","aliases":["Dance"],"photos":[{"src":"/.netlify/functions/access?action=media&name=f96a3d75d2958ca54aa4a7eb.webp","credit":"Henri Matisse","license":"Public domain","sourceUrl":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Matissedance.jpg","caption":"Identified work. Sculpture photographs may show later casts or surviving copies. Shown: Dance (Hermitage, 1910) · 1910"}],"questionIds":[],"tapestryIds":["t68-f305751c9b61"],"museumIds":[],"mapIds":[],"note":"The large 1910 version emphasises rhythm, simplified bodies and strong colour; an earlier version exists.","creator":"Henri Matisse"},{"id":"LE102-7fd7aeda3a00239b","title":"Mexican Revolution begins","kind":"history","reference":"https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?search=Mexican%20Revolution%20begins","aliases":["Mexican Revolution begins"],"photos":[],"questionIds":["ARCHED-NEW101-0534"],"tapestryIds":["t68-ddba969b1961"],"museumIds":[],"mapIds":[],"note":"A prolonged revolution involving different movements, leaders and competing social programmes."},{"id":"LE102-4b1205b70eba35f3","title":"Abstraction versus non-objective art","kind":"art","reference":"https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?search=Abstraction%20versus%20non-objective%20art","aliases":["Abstraction versus non-objective art"],"photos":[],"questionIds":[],"tapestryIds":["t69-e83acf02b8a7"],"museumIds":[],"mapIds":[],"note":"Abstraction may transform a recognisable subject; non-objective art need not start from one. Do not use abstract as a synonym for every modern artwork."},{"id":"LE102-6adef7f30ebf3927","title":"Dynamism of a Dog on a Leash","kind":"art","reference":"https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?search=Dynamism%20of%20a%20Dog%20on%20a%20Leash","aliases":["Dynamism of a Dog on a Leash"],"photos":[{"src":"/.netlify/functions/access?action=media&name=94dbd45784b54737e525963c.webp","credit":"Giacomo Balla","license":"Copyrighted artwork; reproduction from Wikipedia. Commercial-use permission not established.","sourceUrl":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:Giacomo_Balla%2C_1912%2C_Dynamism_of_a_Dog_on_a_Leash%2C_oil_on_canvas%2C_89.8_x_109.8_cm%2C_Albright-Knox_Art_Gallery.jpg","caption":"Identified work. Sculpture photographs may show later casts or surviving copies."},{"src":"/.netlify/functions/access?action=media&name=94dbd45784b54737e525963c.webp","credit":"Giacomo Balla","license":"Copyrighted artwork; reproduction from Wikipedia. Commercial-use permission not established.","sourceUrl":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:Giacomo_Balla%2C_1912%2C_Dynamism_of_a_Dog_on_a_Leash%2C_oil_on_canvas%2C_89.8_x_109.8_cm%2C_Albright-Knox_Art_Gallery.jpg","licenseUrl":""},{"src":"/.netlify/functions/access?action=media&name=94dbd45784b54737e525963c.webp","credit":"Giacomo Balla","license":"Copyrighted artwork; reproduction from Wikipedia. Commercial-use permission not established.","sourceUrl":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:Giacomo_Balla%2C_1912%2C_Dynamism_of_a_Dog_on_a_Leash%2C_oil_on_canvas%2C_89.8_x_109.8_cm%2C_Albright-Knox_Art_Gallery.jpg","licenseUrl":""}],"questionIds":["GEN43-Q01251","ALPHA-B009-Q788","PDF33-Q096-A"],"tapestryIds":["t68-c8f1ada187ec"],"museumIds":["ART93-t68-c8f1ada187ec"],"mapIds":[],"note":"Repeated forms suggest motion and the influence of photographic studies.","creator":"Giacomo Balla","assetIds":["ART93-t68-c8f1ada187ec","T81-t68-c8f1ada187ec"]},{"id":"LE102-40078716206e4efb","title":"French protectorate established in Morocco","kind":"history","reference":"https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?search=French%20protectorate%20established%20in%20Morocco","aliases":["French protectorate established in Morocco"],"photos":[],"questionIds":["ARCHED-NEW101-0495"],"tapestryIds":["t68-0f6702c28a37"],"museumIds":[],"mapIds":[],"note":"The Treaty of Fez formalised the protectorate; the source's 1909 marker is not the treaty date."},{"id":"LE102-6d054d0beb80cc83","title":"Titanic sinks","kind":"history","reference":"https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?search=Titanic%20sinks","aliases":["Titanic sinks"],"photos":[],"questionIds":[],"tapestryIds":["t68-e98200a2e216"],"museumIds":[],"mapIds":[],"note":"The passenger liner sank on its maiden voyage after striking an iceberg."},{"id":"LE102-4d2c094c598c4172","title":"Jackson Pollock","kind":"person","reference":"https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?search=Jackson%20Pollock","aliases":["Jackson Pollock"],"photos":[],"questionIds":["ALPHA-B004-Q311","PDF34-Q-109-B","PDF34-CON-023-A"],"tapestryIds":["t68-60f4050324b8"],"museumIds":[],"mapIds":[],"note":"Abstract Expressionist painter known for poured and dripped compositions."},{"id":"LE102-4f8c593259dcf707","title":"Composition VII","kind":"art","reference":"https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?search=Composition%20VII","aliases":["Composition VII"],"photos":[{"src":"/.netlify/functions/access?action=media&name=4dee69a6f481824acd48c495.webp","credit":"Wassily Kandinsky","license":"Public domain","sourceUrl":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Composition_VII_-_Wassily_Kandinsky,_GAC.jpg","caption":"Identified work. Sculpture photographs may show later casts or surviving copies. Shown: Composition VII · 1913"},{"src":"/.netlify/functions/access?action=media&name=4dee69a6f481824acd48c495.webp","credit":"Wassily Kandinsky","license":"Public domain","sourceUrl":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Composition_VII_-_Wassily_Kandinsky,_GAC.jpg","licenseUrl":""}],"questionIds":["ADD45-Q11507"],"tapestryIds":["t68-acc8cc2ed3af"],"museumIds":["PDFART48-194"],"mapIds":[],"note":"An abstract composition; the sheet says Composition without a number, so this is contextual rather than an exact identification.","creator":"Wassily Kandinsky","assetIds":["PDFART48-194"]},{"id":"LE102-3c04deaa94b7fb7c","title":"Dynamism of a Cyclist","kind":"art","reference":"https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?search=Dynamism%20of%20a%20Cyclist","aliases":["Dynamism of a Cyclist"],"photos":[{"src":"/.netlify/functions/access?action=media&name=4c063c9346a211f62d2d9438.webp","credit":"Umberto Boccioni","license":"Public domain","sourceUrl":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Umberto_Boccioni%2C_1913%2C_Dynamism_of_a_Cyclist_%28Dinamismo_di_un_ciclista%29%2C_oil_on_canvas%2C_70_x_95_cm%2C_Gianni_Mattioli_Collection%2C_on_long-term_loan_to_the_Peggy_Guggenheim_Collection%2C_Venice.jpg","caption":"Identified work. Sculpture photographs may show later casts or surviving copies."},{"src":"/.netlify/functions/access?action=media&name=4c063c9346a211f62d2d9438.webp","credit":"Umberto Boccioni","license":"Public domain","sourceUrl":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Umberto_Boccioni%2C_1913%2C_Dynamism_of_a_Cyclist_%28Dinamismo_di_un_ciclista%29%2C_oil_on_canvas%2C_70_x_95_cm%2C_Gianni_Mattioli_Collection%2C_on_long-term_loan_to_the_Peggy_Guggenheim_Collection%2C_Venice.jpg","licenseUrl":""}],"questionIds":["ALPHA-B004-Q294"],"tapestryIds":["t68-8f7ccc2d89be"],"museumIds":["ART93-t68-8f7ccc2d89be"],"mapIds":[],"note":"Futurist painting explores movement rather than depicting a static anatomical study.","creator":"Umberto Boccioni","assetIds":["ART93-t68-8f7ccc2d89be"]},{"id":"LE102-f6c48507cbe10ec4","title":"Unique Forms of Continuity in Space","kind":"art","reference":"https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?search=Unique%20Forms%20of%20Continuity%20in%20Space","aliases":["Unique Forms of Continuity in Space"],"photos":[{"src":"/.netlify/functions/access?action=media&name=b4c5f23d0e986f9d75e06d68.webp","credit":"Umberto Boccioni","license":"Image © respective rights holders · MoMA collection","sourceUrl":"https://www.moma.org/collection/works/81179","caption":"Identified work. Sculpture photographs may show later casts or surviving copies. Shown: Unique Forms of Continuity in Space · 1913 (cast 1931 or 1934)"},{"src":"/.netlify/functions/access?action=media&name=b4c5f23d0e986f9d75e06d68.webp","credit":"The Museum of Modern Art, New York · Acquired through the Lillie P. Bliss Bequest (by exchange)","license":"Image © respective rights holders · MoMA collection","sourceUrl":"https://www.moma.org/collection/works/81179","licenseUrl":"https://www.moma.org/collection/works/81179"},{"src":"/.netlify/functions/access?action=media&name=b4c5f23d0e986f9d75e06d68.webp","credit":"Umberto Boccioni","license":"Image © respective rights holders · MoMA collection","sourceUrl":"https://www.moma.org/collection/works/81179","licenseUrl":""}],"questionIds":["GEN43-Q01035","GEN43-Q01252","DER-Q708-DYNAMISM","PDF35-Q034-A"],"tapestryIds":["t68-054b0dcf090f"],"museumIds":["M77-MOMA-81179"],"mapIds":[],"note":"Futurist sculpture evokes movement; original plaster and later bronze casts have different dates.","creator":"Umberto Boccioni","assetIds":["M77-MOMA-81179","T81-t68-054b0dcf090f"]},{"id":"LE102-6bf567611a07c5ea","title":"Assassination of Franz Ferdinand in Sarajevo","kind":"history","reference":"https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?search=Assassination%20of%20Franz%20Ferdinand%20in%20Sarajevo","aliases":["Assassination of Franz Ferdinand in Sarajevo"],"photos":[],"questionIds":["ARCHED-NEW101-0486"],"tapestryIds":["t68-7c2bcb191c97"],"museumIds":[],"mapIds":[],"note":"The assassination on 28 June triggered the July Crisis; it was not the sole underlying cause of the war."},{"id":"LE102-1465d156361b316f","title":"Battle of Tannenberg","kind":"history","reference":"https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?search=Battle%20of%20Tannenberg","aliases":["Battle of Tannenberg"],"photos":[],"questionIds":[],"tapestryIds":["t68-7c2e152df39f"],"museumIds":[],"mapIds":[],"note":"A German victory over Russian forces on the Eastern Front."},{"id":"LE102-82357a36d2c6f22e","title":"First Battle of the Marne","kind":"history","reference":"https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?search=First%20Battle%20of%20the%20Marne","aliases":["First Battle of the Marne"],"photos":[],"questionIds":[],"tapestryIds":["t68-6511e477694f"],"museumIds":[],"mapIds":[],"note":"Stopped the German advance towards Paris; followed by prolonged trench warfare."},{"id":"LE102-ab594bb5b6bb2f1f","title":"Mystery and Melancholy of a Street","kind":"art","reference":"https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?search=Mystery%20and%20Melancholy%20of%20a%20Street","aliases":["Mystery and Melancholy of a Street"],"photos":[{"src":"/.netlify/functions/access?action=media&name=f700664876abdd3751ae799c.webp","credit":"Giorgio de Chirico","license":"Copyrighted artwork; reproduction from Wikipedia. Commercial-use permission not established.","sourceUrl":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:Giorgio_de_Chirico_-_Mystery_and_Melancholy_of_a_Street_%281914%29.jpg","caption":"Identified work. Sculpture photographs may show later casts or surviving copies."}],"questionIds":[],"tapestryIds":["t68-62af444df3e5"],"museumIds":[],"mapIds":[],"note":"Arcades, shadows and an isolated figure produce the enigmatic atmosphere of Metaphysical painting.","creator":"Giorgio de Chirico"},{"id":"LE102-8e3f79ba62fc69af","title":"Panama Canal opens","kind":"history","reference":"https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?search=Panama%20Canal%20opens","aliases":["Panama Canal opens"],"photos":[],"questionIds":[],"tapestryIds":["t68-c342f86a53d1"],"museumIds":[],"mapIds":[],"note":"The canal connected Atlantic and Pacific shipping routes."},{"id":"LE102-ec229236f9c8b8ed","title":"First World War","kind":"history","reference":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/World_War_I","aliases":["First World War"],"photos":[],"questionIds":["GEN43-Q03820","GEN43-Q03821","GEN43-Q03822","GEN43-Q04423","ARCHED-B03-20261007-355","ARCHED-NEW99-0243","ARCHED-NEW99-0271","ARCHED-NEW99-0626","ARCHED-NEW99-0950","ARCHED-NEW101-0155","ALPHA-B001-Q081","ALPHA-B008-Q741","PDF35-Q056-A"],"tapestryIds":["t68-3b66dca6d225"],"museumIds":[],"mapIds":[],"note":"Industrial warfare, rival alliances and imperial competition transformed Europe; the Western Front armistice was 11 November 1918."},{"id":"LE102-2958c7573925ae51","title":"Black Square","kind":"art","reference":"https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?search=Black%20Square","aliases":["Black Square"],"photos":[{"src":"/.netlify/functions/access?action=media&name=0fdf38d28b955a875cc4f440.webp","credit":"Kazimir Malevich","license":"Public domain","sourceUrl":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Kazimir_Malevich%2C_1915%2C_Black_Suprematic_Square%2C_oil_on_linen_canvas%2C_79.5_x_79.5_cm%2C_Tretyakov_Gallery%2C_Moscow.jpg","caption":"Identified work. Sculpture photographs may show later casts or surviving copies."},{"src":"/.netlify/functions/access?action=media&name=0fdf38d28b955a875cc4f440.webp","credit":"Kazimir Malevich","license":"Public domain","sourceUrl":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Kazimir_Malevich%2C_1915%2C_Black_Suprematic_Square%2C_oil_on_linen_canvas%2C_79.5_x_79.5_cm%2C_Tretyakov_Gallery%2C_Moscow.jpg","licenseUrl":""}],"questionIds":["GEN43-Q03738"],"tapestryIds":["t68-6c737be7c36c"],"museumIds":[],"mapIds":[],"note":"A foundational Suprematist work; multiple later versions exist.","creator":"Kazimir Malevich","assetIds":["T81-t68-6c737be7c36c"]},{"id":"LE102-259267c5fd4d9b8e","title":"Treaty of London","kind":"history","reference":"https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?search=Treaty%20of%20London","aliases":["Treaty of London"],"photos":[],"questionIds":["GEN43-Q04163","ARCHED-NEW101-0487"],"tapestryIds":["t68-90266f628f28"],"museumIds":[],"mapIds":[],"note":"Secret Allied promises preceded Italy's entry into the war against Austria-Hungary."},{"id":"LE102-0060d2924bd5b332","title":"Hussein–McMahon correspondence","kind":"history","reference":"https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?search=Hussein%E2%80%93McMahon%20correspondence","aliases":["Hussein–McMahon correspondence"],"photos":[],"questionIds":[],"tapestryIds":["t68-9c42dfd259ec"],"museumIds":[],"mapIds":[],"note":"Wartime correspondence over Arab independence contained disputed territorial interpretations."},{"id":"LE102-1b1c0254a696af57","title":"Suprematism and Constructivism","kind":"art","reference":"https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?search=Suprematism%20and%20Constructivism","aliases":["Suprematism and Constructivism"],"photos":[],"questionIds":[],"tapestryIds":["t69-bfc75352d2b3"],"museumIds":[],"mapIds":[],"note":"Suprematism emphasises autonomous geometric form; Constructivist practices often connect materials, construction and social production. The movements overlap historically but are not identical."},{"id":"LE102-e314b9bd2d28b529","title":"Dada emerges in Zurich","kind":"art","reference":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Dada","aliases":["Dada emerges in Zurich"],"photos":[],"questionIds":[],"tapestryIds":["t68-a3b355f60704"],"museumIds":[],"mapIds":[],"note":"Wartime anti-establishment experimentation; Dada developed differently across cities.","creator":"Hugo Ball, Tristan Tzara"},{"id":"LE102-11ff566adf7f4eeb","title":"Sykes–Picot Agreement","kind":"history","reference":"https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?search=Sykes%E2%80%93Picot%20Agreement","aliases":["Sykes–Picot Agreement"],"photos":[],"questionIds":[],"tapestryIds":["t68-001d434ddfa1"],"museumIds":[],"mapIds":[],"note":"A secret agreement envisaged spheres of influence in Ottoman Arab territories."},{"id":"LE102-5dd1f8592a5552e3","title":"Readymade and the artist's act of selection","kind":"art","reference":"https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?search=Readymade%20and%20the%20artist%27s%20act%20of%20selection","aliases":["Readymade and the artist's act of selection"],"photos":[],"questionIds":[],"tapestryIds":["t69-771f86f10b7b"],"museumIds":[],"mapIds":[],"note":"A manufactured object can enter art through selection and presentation. A readymade is not simply a sculpture made from any unusual material."},{"id":"LE102-64cdc9e3fc08be09","title":"Balfour Declaration","kind":"history","reference":"https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?search=Balfour%20Declaration","aliases":["Balfour Declaration"],"photos":[],"questionIds":[],"tapestryIds":["t68-d5fa5d8c1bbc"],"museumIds":[],"mapIds":[],"note":"British support for a national home for the Jewish people in Palestine included a clause on the rights of existing non-Jewish communities."},{"id":"LE102-02b7d742a8330207","title":"Russian February and October Revolutions","kind":"history","reference":"https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?search=Russian%20February%20and%20October%20Revolutions","aliases":["Russian February and October Revolutions"],"photos":[],"questionIds":["ARCHED-NEW101-0506"],"tapestryIds":["t68-fc58ae0e61bc"],"museumIds":[],"mapIds":[],"note":"Tsarist rule fell, followed by Bolshevik seizure of power; calendar conventions explain the month names."},{"id":"LE102-d7143d20518bcd4f","title":"United States enters World War I","kind":"history","reference":"https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?search=United%20States%20enters%20World%20War%20I","aliases":["United States enters World War I"],"photos":[],"questionIds":["ARCHED-NEW101-0484"],"tapestryIds":["t68-0412ff8a53cd"],"museumIds":[],"mapIds":[],"note":"US entry in April altered Allied resources and the diplomatic balance."},{"id":"LE102-6e55d720949b5e5b","title":"De Stijl and Neo-Plasticism","kind":"art","reference":"https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?search=De%20Stijl%20and%20Neo-Plasticism","aliases":["De Stijl and Neo-Plasticism"],"photos":[],"questionIds":[],"tapestryIds":["t69-ad44ece2e4a6"],"museumIds":[],"mapIds":[],"note":"Restricted colour, orthogonal relationships and compositional balance link painting, furniture and architecture. Mondrian's painting and Rietveld's buildings are distinct applications."},{"id":"LE102-d051f3a101f9e6c1","title":"Armistice of 11 November","kind":"history","reference":"https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?search=Armistice%20of%2011%20November","aliases":["Armistice of 11 November"],"photos":[],"questionIds":[],"tapestryIds":["t68-9cb6fe7c4591"],"museumIds":[],"mapIds":[],"note":"Ended fighting between Germany and the Allies; the peace treaty followed in 1919."},{"id":"LE102-a00f033aa2cc3b90","title":"White on White","kind":"art","reference":"https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?search=White%20on%20White","aliases":["White on White"],"photos":[{"src":"/.netlify/functions/access?action=media&name=37a5da4d0a9b973c1a314cca.webp","credit":"Kazimir Malevich","license":"Image © respective rights holders · MoMA collection","sourceUrl":"https://www.moma.org/collection/works/80385","caption":"Identified work. Sculpture photographs may show later casts or surviving copies. Shown: Suprematist Composition: White on White · 1918"}],"questionIds":["PDF33-Q098-A"],"tapestryIds":["t68-e0edde4a13f5"],"museumIds":[],"mapIds":[],"note":"Suprematist painting reduces form and colour to subtle relationships.","creator":"Kazimir Malevich"},{"id":"LE102-f3fb3ca86141199f","title":"Wilson's Fourteen Points","kind":"history","reference":"https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?search=Wilson%27s%20Fourteen%20Points","aliases":["Wilson's Fourteen Points"],"photos":[],"questionIds":["ARCHED-NEW101-0497","ARCHED-NEW101-0522"],"tapestryIds":["t68-d7872ffe7487"],"museumIds":[],"mapIds":[],"note":"A programme for peace; the eventual treaties did not adopt all of its principles."},{"id":"LE102-748226d9fde0173a","title":"D'Annunzio occupies Fiume","kind":"history","reference":"https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?search=D%27Annunzio%20occupies%20Fiume","aliases":["D'Annunzio occupies Fiume"],"photos":[],"questionIds":[],"tapestryIds":["t68-7b8d77565445"],"museumIds":[],"mapIds":[],"note":"A nationalist occupation challenged the postwar settlement; distinguish from the 1924 annexation treaty."},{"id":"LE102-70729af5373a5ac6","title":"Paris Peace Conference","kind":"history","reference":"https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?search=Paris%20Peace%20Conference","aliases":["Paris Peace Conference"],"photos":[],"questionIds":["ARCHED-NEW101-0531"],"tapestryIds":["t68-de0ef9a9ea79"],"museumIds":[],"mapIds":[],"note":"The conference negotiated several treaties and the League of Nations framework."},{"id":"LE102-aefe377b6f8655ef","title":"Treaty of Versailles","kind":"history","reference":"https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?search=Treaty%20of%20Versailles","aliases":["Treaty of Versailles"],"photos":[],"questionIds":["ARCHED-B100-20261007-055"],"tapestryIds":["t68-d7be04437461"],"museumIds":[],"mapIds":[],"note":"The German peace settlement imposed territorial, military and financial terms."},{"id":"LE102-3645ee0f08489c31","title":"Weimar Constitution adopted","kind":"history","reference":"https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?search=Weimar%20Constitution%20adopted","aliases":["Weimar Constitution adopted"],"photos":[],"questionIds":["ARCHED-NEW101-0500"],"tapestryIds":["t68-4036d07208cd"],"museumIds":[],"mapIds":[],"note":"Established Germany's parliamentary republic; later collapse was not inevitable at its founding."},{"id":"LE102-eb3c4b0a04c3449b","title":"Spatial Construction: series","kind":"art","reference":"https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?search=Spatial%20Construction%3A%20series","aliases":["Spatial Construction: series"],"photos":[{"src":"/.netlify/functions/access?action=media&name=a64c2073c03ac8db1ca343c1.webp","credit":"Naum Gabo","license":"CC0","sourceUrl":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Kuspit3-27-2.jpg","caption":"Contextual example: Gabo's Kinetic Construction (Standing Wave), 1919–1920, shown through documentation/reconstruction. The source's generic Spatial Construction title remains unresolved."}],"questionIds":[],"tapestryIds":["t68-76a9835e0445"],"museumIds":[],"mapIds":[],"note":"Constructivist exploration of space; the source does not securely specify one construction.","creator":"Naum Gabo"},{"id":"LE102-15ade214b140695e","title":"Bauhaus school","kind":"history","reference":"https://www.bauhaus.de/de/das_bauhaus/","aliases":["Bauhaus school"],"photos":[],"questionIds":["GEN43-Q01022","GEN43-Q01023","PDF35-CON-016-A"],"tapestryIds":["t68-0e4ffd289c59"],"museumIds":[],"mapIds":[],"note":"Founded in Weimar, moved to Dessau and then Berlin; closed under Nazi pressure in 1933.","built":"1919","creator":"Walter Gropius, Hannes Meyer, Ludwig Mies van der Rohe","resolvedTitle102":"Bauhaus Dessau"},{"id":"LE102-25feb64202403cce","title":"Bauhaus: workshop, industry and changing directors","kind":"architecture","reference":"https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?search=Bauhaus","aliases":["Bauhaus: workshop, industry and changing directors"],"photos":[],"questionIds":[],"tapestryIds":["t69-ba09c05d63cd"],"museumIds":[],"mapIds":[],"note":"Gropius, Meyer and Mies led different phases. The school changed location and priorities; Bauhaus cannot be reduced to one fixed visual style.","built":"1919"},{"id":"LE102-fca189d134d2f975","title":"Bloody Christmas in Fiume","kind":"history","reference":"https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?search=Bloody%20Christmas%20in%20Fiume","aliases":["Bloody Christmas in Fiume"],"photos":[],"questionIds":["ARCHED-NEW101-0518"],"tapestryIds":["t68-5b8ffc30b278"],"museumIds":[],"mapIds":[],"note":"Italian forces ended D'Annunzio's occupation in December."},{"id":"LE102-466e74e770d38407","title":"League of Nations begins operating","kind":"history","reference":"https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?search=League%20of%20Nations%20begins%20operating","aliases":["League of Nations begins operating"],"photos":[],"questionIds":["ARCHED-NEW101-0459","ARCHED-NEW101-0528"],"tapestryIds":["t68-733f9bef18b3"],"museumIds":[],"mapIds":[],"note":"An attempt at collective security after World War I; the United States did not join."},{"id":"LE102-379dfb8dd77ffbaa","title":"Curtain wall versus load-bearing wall","kind":"architecture","reference":"https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?search=Curtain%20wall%20versus%20load-bearing%20wall","aliases":["Curtain wall versus load-bearing wall"],"photos":[],"questionIds":[],"tapestryIds":["t69-c4589956dda7"],"museumIds":[],"mapIds":[],"note":"A curtain wall encloses a building while the structural frame carries primary loads. A glass facade is not automatically a curtain wall.","built":"1920"},{"id":"LE102-8eb0201ca080c00c","title":"International Style and modernist diversity","kind":"architecture","reference":"https://www.vam.ac.uk/articles/what-was-modernism","aliases":["International Style and modernist diversity"],"photos":[],"questionIds":[],"tapestryIds":["t69-192da3928b42"],"museumIds":[],"mapIds":[],"note":"The 1932 exhibition and book popularised a formal category. Functionalism, social housing programmes and regional modernisms cannot all be reduced to that category.","built":"1920"},{"id":"LE102-5f4f6b58b549dcea","title":"Italian Rationalism and political context","kind":"architecture","reference":"https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?search=Italian%20Rationalism%20and%20political%20context","aliases":["Italian Rationalism and political context"],"photos":[],"questionIds":[],"tapestryIds":["t69-20e8ced6fa6d"],"museumIds":[],"mapIds":[],"note":"Geometric clarity and modern materials coexisted with Fascist commissions. Formal innovation alone does not identify the politics of a patron or architect.","built":"1920"},{"id":"LE102-c7cea3e6708443a1","title":"Pilotis, free plan and free facade","kind":"architecture","reference":"https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?search=Pilotis%2C%20free%20plan%20and%20free%20facade","aliases":["Pilotis, free plan and free facade"],"photos":[],"questionIds":[],"tapestryIds":["t69-0d2232f0f090"],"museumIds":[],"mapIds":[],"note":"Le Corbusier's Five Points also include horizontal windows and roof gardens. A frame separates structural support from partitions and the external enclosure.","built":"1920"},{"id":"LE102-731b284eec78faaf","title":"Reinforced concrete and cantilevers","kind":"architecture","reference":"https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?search=Reinforced%20concrete%20and%20cantilevers","aliases":["Reinforced concrete and cantilevers"],"photos":[],"questionIds":[],"tapestryIds":["t69-8e1fda07f8be"],"museumIds":[],"mapIds":[],"note":"Steel reinforcement helps concrete resist tensile forces. A cantilever projects beyond its support; its structural action differs from a simple span supported at both ends.","built":"1920"},{"id":"LE102-6058c606d84a3588","title":"March on Rome","kind":"history","reference":"https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?search=March%20on%20Rome","aliases":["March on Rome"],"photos":[],"questionIds":["ALPHA-B005-Q444"],"tapestryIds":["t68-80fb824aad6d"],"museumIds":[],"mapIds":[],"note":"Fascist pressure preceded the king's appointment of Mussolini as prime minister; dictatorship consolidated later."},{"id":"LE102-e02c8e7fe83713c8","title":"Soviet Union founded","kind":"history","reference":"https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?search=Soviet%20Union%20founded","aliases":["Soviet Union founded"],"photos":[],"questionIds":[],"tapestryIds":["t68-683799ff4039"],"museumIds":[],"mapIds":[],"note":"The USSR was established in December 1922, not in 1917."},{"id":"LE102-be67929472f001ba","title":"French and Belgian occupation of the Ruhr","kind":"history","reference":"https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?search=French%20and%20Belgian%20occupation%20of%20the%20Ruhr","aliases":["French and Belgian occupation of the Ruhr"],"photos":[],"questionIds":[],"tapestryIds":["t68-8c8ca2588103"],"museumIds":[],"mapIds":[],"note":"A reparations crisis intensified economic and political instability in Germany."},{"id":"LE102-f050205859b305b5","title":"Republic of Turkey proclaimed","kind":"history","reference":"https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?search=Republic%20of%20Turkey%20proclaimed","aliases":["Republic of Turkey proclaimed"],"photos":[],"questionIds":["ARCHED-NEW101-0467"],"tapestryIds":["t68-21db2b536832"],"museumIds":[],"mapIds":[],"note":"Atatürk's republic followed the collapse of the Ottoman Empire and a war of independence."},{"id":"LE102-bc14043b10622ff9","title":"Roy Lichtenstein","kind":"person","reference":"https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?search=Roy%20Lichtenstein","aliases":["Roy Lichtenstein"],"photos":[],"questionIds":["GEN43-Q03735","ALPHA-B002-Q114","PDF33-Q107-B"],"tapestryIds":["t68-49259928cc80"],"museumIds":[],"mapIds":[],"note":"American Pop artist drawing on commercial printing and comics."},{"id":"LE102-d76bc9e5a5603460","title":"Dawes Plan","kind":"history","reference":"https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?search=Dawes%20Plan","aliases":["Dawes Plan"],"photos":[],"questionIds":["ARCHED-NEW101-0123","ARCHED-NEW101-0456","ARCHED-NEW101-0463","ARCHED-NEW101-0487"],"tapestryIds":["t68-f6ee02824c7c"],"museumIds":[],"mapIds":[],"note":"Restructured German reparations payments and encouraged US loans."},{"id":"LE102-4d9ada7daa0681c6","title":"Matteotti murdered and Aventine Secession","kind":"history","reference":"https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?search=Matteotti%20murdered%20and%20Aventine%20Secession","aliases":["Matteotti murdered and Aventine Secession"],"photos":[],"questionIds":[],"tapestryIds":["t68-e90aa082f91e"],"museumIds":[],"mapIds":[],"note":"The socialist deputy's murder provoked an opposition withdrawal; the crisis preceded consolidation of Fascist dictatorship."},{"id":"LE102-5f818594066845ba","title":"Surrealist Manifesto published","kind":"art","reference":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Surrealist_Manifesto","aliases":["Surrealist Manifesto published"],"photos":[],"questionIds":[],"tapestryIds":["t68-9fbfe699f824"],"museumIds":[],"mapIds":[],"note":"An organised movement explored dreams, automatism and the unconscious.","creator":"André Breton"},{"id":"LE102-7297747a0cf6c742","title":"Treaty of Rome on Fiume","kind":"history","reference":"https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?search=Treaty%20of%20Rome%20on%20Fiume","aliases":["Treaty of Rome on Fiume"],"photos":[],"questionIds":[],"tapestryIds":["t68-306f01e1a89c"],"museumIds":[],"mapIds":[],"note":"Fiume passed to Italy; distinguish this agreement from the European integration treaties of 1957."},{"id":"LE102-7c9382f84893461e","title":"Surrealist automatism and dream imagery","kind":"art","reference":"https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?search=Surrealist%20automatism%20and%20dream%20imagery","aliases":["Surrealist automatism and dream imagery"],"photos":[],"questionIds":[],"tapestryIds":["t69-a966abfd1d69"],"museumIds":[],"mapIds":[],"note":"Automatism reduces deliberate control; illusionistic dream imagery is another Surrealist strategy. Dalí's detailed rendering should not stand for every Surrealist method."},{"id":"LE102-ffecc4e9f62a31b5","title":"Locarno Treaties","kind":"history","reference":"https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?search=Locarno%20Treaties","aliases":["Locarno Treaties"],"photos":[],"questionIds":["GEN43-Q01283","ARCHED-NEW101-0479"],"tapestryIds":["t68-07c84a5aabbe"],"museumIds":[],"mapIds":[],"note":"Diplomatic agreements guaranteed Germany's western borders; eastern borders did not receive identical guarantees."},{"id":"LE102-01a2b76f025f5d92","title":"Yellow–Red–Blue","kind":"art","reference":"https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?search=Yellow%E2%80%93Red%E2%80%93Blue","aliases":["Yellow–Red–Blue"],"photos":[{"src":"/.netlify/functions/access?action=media&name=021a9fd650384cc773e741a5.webp","credit":"Wassily Kandinsky","license":"Public domain","sourceUrl":"https://it.wikipedia.org/wiki/Giallo%2C_rosso%2C_blu","caption":"Exact title and artist matched to existing catalogue"}],"questionIds":[],"tapestryIds":["t68-db291121a832"],"museumIds":[],"mapIds":[],"note":"Painted during Kandinsky's Bauhaus period; structured geometry coexists with freer forms.","creator":"Wassily Kandinsky"},{"id":"LE102-0c72d1ba6f256741","title":"Robert Rauschenberg","kind":"person","reference":"https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?search=Robert%20Rauschenberg","aliases":["Robert Rauschenberg"],"photos":[],"questionIds":[],"tapestryIds":["t68-ea3348df8766"],"museumIds":[],"mapIds":[],"note":"American artist whose Combines connect painting, sculpture and everyday objects."},{"id":"LE102-189341f5acc15e0e","title":"Baird demonstrates television","kind":"history","reference":"https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?search=Baird%20demonstrates%20television","aliases":["Baird demonstrates television"],"photos":[],"questionIds":["ARCHED-NEW101-0468"],"tapestryIds":["t68-5c9994310026"],"museumIds":[],"mapIds":[],"note":"A public demonstration of a working television system; broadcasting developed in later stages."},{"id":"LE102-b2602b93700f212d","title":"Fleming discovers penicillin's antibacterial effect","kind":"history","reference":"https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?search=Fleming%20discovers%20penicillin%27s%20antibacterial%20effect","aliases":["Fleming discovers penicillin's antibacterial effect"],"photos":[],"questionIds":["ARCHED-NEW101-0533"],"tapestryIds":["t68-568766a50cc2"],"museumIds":[],"mapIds":[],"note":"Clinical production and widespread use required later work by other researchers."},{"id":"LE102-f3c88bf1d1a87211","title":"Kellogg–Briand Pact","kind":"history","reference":"https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?search=Kellogg%E2%80%93Briand%20Pact","aliases":["Kellogg–Briand Pact"],"photos":[],"questionIds":["GEN43-Q01284","ARCHED-NEW101-0481"],"tapestryIds":["t68-67e5463898ca"],"museumIds":[],"mapIds":[],"note":"Signatories renounced war as national policy; enforcement proved weak."},{"id":"LE102-d4e16fefd2136914","title":"Yves Klein","kind":"person","reference":"https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?search=Yves%20Klein","aliases":["Yves Klein"],"photos":[],"questionIds":[],"tapestryIds":["t68-3cdde3e2aa3f"],"museumIds":[],"mapIds":[],"note":"French artist associated with monochromes, performance and Nouveau Réalisme."},{"id":"LE102-fc2a24b5812a6e96","title":"Andy Warhol","kind":"person","reference":"https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?search=Andy%20Warhol","aliases":["Andy Warhol"],"photos":[],"questionIds":["GEN43-Q04364","ALPHA-B004-Q331","ALPHA-B006-Q596","ALPHA-B009-Q788","PDF33-Q106-B"],"tapestryIds":["t68-63be63ca87c0"],"museumIds":[],"mapIds":[],"note":"American Pop artist investigating celebrity, consumption and serial reproduction."},{"id":"LE102-26614c946bf527fd","title":"Lateran Pacts","kind":"history","reference":"https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?search=Lateran%20Pacts","aliases":["Lateran Pacts"],"photos":[],"questionIds":["GEN43-Q04169","ARCHED-NEW101-0486","ARCHED-NEW101-0522"],"tapestryIds":["t68-c21f1a149bd4"],"museumIds":[],"mapIds":[],"note":"Settled the Roman Question and created Vatican City as a sovereign state."},{"id":"LE102-6b4f26f07b5da08d","title":"The Treachery of Images","kind":"art","reference":"https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?search=The%20Treachery%20of%20Images","aliases":["The Treachery of Images"],"photos":[{"src":"/.netlify/functions/access?action=media&name=7b07a3ccfa3a0e05ec806e8e.webp","credit":"Los Angeles County Museum of Art · Wikimedia Commons","license":"Public domain","sourceUrl":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/The_Treachery_of_Images","caption":"Exact title and artist matched to existing catalogue"},{"src":"/.netlify/functions/access?action=media&name=2a89825bb8393246487ccf5a.webp","credit":"Los Angeles County Museum of Art · Wikimedia Commons","license":"Public domain","sourceUrl":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Magritte_treachery.jpg","licenseUrl":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/Commons:Licensing"},{"src":"/.netlify/functions/access?action=media&name=7b07a3ccfa3a0e05ec806e8e.webp","credit":"Los Angeles County Museum of Art · Wikimedia Commons","license":"Public domain","sourceUrl":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/The_Treachery_of_Images","licenseUrl":""}],"questionIds":["GEN43-Q01257","ADD45-Q11231","ADD45-Q11232"],"tapestryIds":["t68-a5db25d5c768"],"museumIds":["ART45-Q1061035"],"mapIds":[],"note":"The painted pipe and its text distinguish an object from an image of that object.","creator":"René Magritte","assetIds":["ART45-Q1061035","T81-t68-a5db25d5c768"],"placeId":"MAP103-Q1641836"},{"id":"LE102-5ec4971bb94fa936","title":"Wall Street crash","kind":"history","reference":"https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?search=Wall%20Street%20crash","aliases":["Wall Street crash"],"photos":[],"questionIds":["ARCHED-NEW101-0526"],"tapestryIds":["t68-46cea29fab6a"],"museumIds":[],"mapIds":[],"note":"The stock-market collapse accompanied the onset of the Great Depression; the depression had broader causes."},{"id":"LE102-56f50a0ade597972","title":"Great Depression","kind":"history","reference":"https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?search=Great%20Depression","aliases":["Great Depression"],"photos":[],"questionIds":["ALPHA-B003-Q224"],"tapestryIds":["t68-118b90acd1ab"],"museumIds":[],"mapIds":[],"note":"A severe global economic crisis; dates of recovery varied by country."},{"id":"LE102-9780d433aa6fbd5d","title":"Composition with Red, Blue and Yellow","kind":"art","reference":"https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?search=Composition%20with%20Red%2C%20Blue%20and%20Yellow","aliases":["Composition with Red, Blue and Yellow"],"photos":[{"src":"/.netlify/functions/access?action=media&name=6db128e83ed9104ae4e2ff51.webp","credit":"Piet Mondrian","license":"Public domain","sourceUrl":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Piet_Mondriaan%2C_1930_-_Mondrian_Composition_II_in_Red%2C_Blue%2C_and_Yellow.jpg","caption":"Identified work. Sculpture photographs may show later casts or surviving copies."}],"questionIds":[],"tapestryIds":["t68-f4a4ab79d2b5"],"museumIds":[],"mapIds":[],"note":"A representative Neo-Plasticist composition; the sheet's generic title may refer to another version.","creator":"Piet Mondrian"},{"id":"LE102-13e1134c33db99b1","title":"London Naval Treaty","kind":"history","reference":"https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?search=London%20Naval%20Treaty","aliases":["London Naval Treaty"],"photos":[],"questionIds":[],"tapestryIds":["t68-4abd7840c166"],"museumIds":[],"mapIds":[],"note":"An interwar agreement limiting certain categories of naval armament."},{"id":"LE102-d2c6d89a2cba9a7a","title":"Urban functional zoning and its critics","kind":"architecture","reference":"https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?search=Urban%20functional%20zoning%20and%20its%20critics","aliases":["Urban functional zoning and its critics"],"photos":[],"questionIds":[],"tapestryIds":["t69-e8f327579c04"],"museumIds":[],"mapIds":[],"note":"Separating housing, work, recreation and circulation was influential in modernist planning. Critics later questioned its treatment of street life and mixed uses.","built":"1930"},{"id":"LE102-4f175a68b9925703","title":"Horse and Rider","kind":"art","reference":"https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?search=Horse%20and%20Rider","aliases":["Horse and Rider"],"photos":[{"src":"/.netlify/functions/access?action=media&name=5e3f2b5eca9e16ca09f4f61f.webp","credit":"Marino Marini","license":"Image © respective rights holders · MoMA collection","sourceUrl":"https://www.moma.org/collection/works/81477","caption":"Representative work from the series/cycle; the timeline range covers the series, not only this image. Shown: Horse and Rider · 1942"},{"src":"/.netlify/functions/access?action=media&name=5e3f2b5eca9e16ca09f4f61f.webp","credit":"The Museum of Modern Art, New York · Frances R. Keech Bequest","license":"Image © respective rights holders · MoMA collection","sourceUrl":"https://www.moma.org/collection/works/81477","licenseUrl":"https://www.moma.org/collection/works/81477"}],"questionIds":["GEN43-Q01301","GEN43-Q02207"],"tapestryIds":["t68-18977c914eba"],"museumIds":["M77-MOMA-81477"],"mapIds":[],"note":"Unresolved series reference: the photo does not identify a specific Marini sculpture. Broad subject period only, not an individual work date.","creator":"Marino Marini","assetIds":["M77-MOMA-81477"]},{"id":"LE102-039f35fbd6f604f1","title":"Statute of Westminster","kind":"history","reference":"https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?search=Statute%20of%20Westminster","aliases":["Statute of Westminster"],"photos":[],"questionIds":["ARCHED-NEW101-0515"],"tapestryIds":["t68-1e52051620b6"],"museumIds":[],"mapIds":[],"note":"Recognised legislative autonomy for specified dominions; implementation differed among them."},{"id":"LE102-85ce86b119942fcc","title":"The Persistence of Memory","kind":"art","reference":"https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?search=The%20Persistence%20of%20Memory","aliases":["The Persistence of Memory"],"photos":[{"src":"/.netlify/functions/access?action=media&name=01fc7f4b00d1d8552112bdb3.webp","credit":"Salvador Dalí · MoMA collection reference","license":"Museum reference · reuse not cleared","sourceUrl":"https://www.moma.org/explore/inside_out/2010/04/14/moma-offsite-where-did-it-go/","caption":"Exact title and artist matched to existing catalogue"},{"src":"/.netlify/functions/access?action=media&name=22eeae45934a421864e9c732.webp","credit":"The Museum of Modern Art, New York · Given anonymously","license":"Image © respective rights holders · MoMA collection","sourceUrl":"https://www.moma.org/collection/works/79018","licenseUrl":"https://www.moma.org/collection/works/79018"}],"questionIds":["ADD45-Q11261","ADD45-Q11262","NEWDER-047","PDF33-Q104-A","PDF34-Q-101-A"],"tapestryIds":["t68-756fd68c687e"],"museumIds":["ART45-OFFICIAL-3d9b2521a7aa"],"mapIds":[],"note":"Precisely painted soft watches unsettle everyday expectations of time and material solidity.","creator":"Salvador Dalí","assetIds":["ART45-OFFICIAL-3d9b2521a7aa"]},{"id":"LE102-4f99dc91d2347320","title":"Kingdom of Saudi Arabia proclaimed","kind":"history","reference":"https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?search=Kingdom%20of%20Saudi%20Arabia%20proclaimed","aliases":["Kingdom of Saudi Arabia proclaimed"],"photos":[],"questionIds":[],"tapestryIds":["t68-d78e7a950abc"],"museumIds":[],"mapIds":[],"note":"Ibn Saud unified his domains under the new kingdom's name."},{"id":"LE102-da6dfe223b92bae1","title":"Woman with Her Throat Cut","kind":"art","reference":"https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?search=Woman%20with%20Her%20Throat%20Cut","aliases":["Woman with Her Throat Cut"],"photos":[{"src":"/.netlify/functions/access?action=media&name=6470eb425193b7116d2933d2.webp","credit":"Alberto Giacometti · The Museum of Modern Art, New York","license":"Copyrighted artwork; image rights retained by source","sourceUrl":"https://www.moma.org/collection/works/81796","caption":"Woman with Her Throat Cut, 1932; the bronze cast photographed by MoMA dates to 1949."},{"src":"/.netlify/functions/access?action=media&name=6470eb425193b7116d2933d2.webp","credit":"Alberto Giacometti · The Museum of Modern Art, New York","license":"Copyrighted artwork; image rights retained by source","sourceUrl":"https://www.moma.org/collection/works/81796","licenseUrl":""}],"questionIds":["GEN43-Q01258"],"tapestryIds":["t68-fd986043a3f8"],"museumIds":[],"mapIds":[],"note":"Giacometti’s Surrealist sculpture evokes violence through an ambiguous bodily form.","creator":"Alberto Giacometti","assetIds":["T81-t68-fd986043a3f8"]},{"id":"LE102-1e75d894978d89af","title":"Germany leaves the League of Nations","kind":"history","reference":"https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?search=Germany%20leaves%20the%20League%20of%20Nations","aliases":["Germany leaves the League of Nations"],"photos":[],"questionIds":[],"tapestryIds":["t68-49a72c608ca2"],"museumIds":[],"mapIds":[],"note":"Withdrawal undermined interwar collective-security arrangements."},{"id":"LE102-6cae66e4e715d92e","title":"Hitler appointed German chancellor","kind":"history","reference":"https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?search=Hitler%20appointed%20German%20chancellor","aliases":["Hitler appointed German chancellor"],"photos":[],"questionIds":[],"tapestryIds":["t68-284440292dc4"],"museumIds":[],"mapIds":[],"note":"Appointed on 30 January; dismantling democracy followed through repression and legislation."},{"id":"LE102-6185158931d8ee21","title":"New Deal begins","kind":"history","reference":"https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?search=New%20Deal%20begins","aliases":["New Deal begins"],"photos":[],"questionIds":[],"tapestryIds":["t68-934d553fd165"],"museumIds":[],"mapIds":[],"note":"Roosevelt's programmes addressed relief, recovery and reform during the Depression."},{"id":"LE102-3f9515bd39708da6","title":"Reichstag fire and emergency decree","kind":"history","reference":"https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?search=Reichstag%20fire%20and%20emergency%20decree","aliases":["Reichstag fire and emergency decree"],"photos":[],"questionIds":["ARCHED-NEW101-0470"],"tapestryIds":["t68-fe1a883bfa01"],"museumIds":[],"mapIds":[],"note":"The fire was used to justify suspension of civil liberties and repression of opponents."},{"id":"LE102-cf14b226437afd77","title":"United States recognises the Soviet Union","kind":"history","reference":"https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?search=United%20States%20recognises%20the%20Soviet%20Union","aliases":["United States recognises the Soviet Union"],"photos":[],"questionIds":[],"tapestryIds":["t68-f109a0396876"],"museumIds":[],"mapIds":[],"note":"Formal diplomatic relations were established under Roosevelt."},{"id":"LE102-6278ba1708c63c04","title":"The Holocaust and Nazi racial persecution","kind":"history","reference":"https://encyclopedia.ushmm.org/content/en/article/final-solution-overview","aliases":["The Holocaust and Nazi racial persecution"],"photos":[],"questionIds":[],"tapestryIds":["t69-46b0189aad99"],"museumIds":[],"mapIds":[],"note":"The systematic murder of six million Jews occurred within wider Nazi persecution and mass killing. Distinguish ghettos, concentration camps and extermination centres."},{"id":"LE102-7cf0ad84c37a2e5c","title":"Dollfuss assassinated in Austrian Nazi coup attempt","kind":"history","reference":"https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?search=Dollfuss%20assassinated%20in%20Austrian%20Nazi%20coup%20attempt","aliases":["Dollfuss assassinated in Austrian Nazi coup attempt"],"photos":[],"questionIds":["ARCHED-NEW101-0460"],"tapestryIds":["t68-af4ce98c2278"],"museumIds":[],"mapIds":[],"note":"The failed coup preceded later Austrian annexation by Germany in 1938."},{"id":"LE102-ff62bbd53f89fc51","title":"Hitler combines presidential and chancellor powers","kind":"history","reference":"https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?search=Hitler%20combines%20presidential%20and%20chancellor%20powers","aliases":["Hitler combines presidential and chancellor powers"],"photos":[],"questionIds":["ARCHED-NEW101-0504"],"tapestryIds":["t68-2b331cc9c1b5"],"museumIds":[],"mapIds":[],"note":"After Hindenburg's death, Hitler consolidated personal dictatorship."},{"id":"LE102-89763294bdac8c6f","title":"Rome Protocols","kind":"history","reference":"https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?search=Rome%20Protocols","aliases":["Rome Protocols"],"photos":[],"questionIds":[],"tapestryIds":["t68-5c474dd65a07"],"museumIds":[],"mapIds":[],"note":"Italy, Austria and Hungary concluded political and economic agreements."},{"id":"LE102-92f3ef09267d3025","title":"Italy invades Ethiopia","kind":"history","reference":"https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?search=Italy%20invades%20Ethiopia","aliases":["Italy invades Ethiopia"],"photos":[],"questionIds":[],"tapestryIds":["t68-e5c4f2cf6eed"],"museumIds":[],"mapIds":[],"note":"The invasion exposed the weakness of League sanctions and expanded Fascist imperial ambitions."},{"id":"LE102-3ac521206203ff8b","title":"Wagner Act","kind":"history","reference":"https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?search=Wagner%20Act","aliases":["Wagner Act"],"photos":[],"questionIds":[],"tapestryIds":["t68-65088d671091"],"museumIds":[],"mapIds":[],"note":"US legislation protected collective bargaining and established a national labour relations framework."},{"id":"LE102-4f7c6b9c279a8195","title":"Christo","kind":"person","reference":"https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?search=Christo","aliases":["Christo"],"photos":[],"questionIds":[],"tapestryIds":["t68-a07191e3e13a"],"museumIds":[],"mapIds":[],"note":"Worked with Jeanne-Claude on temporary large-scale environmental projects; credit the partnership."},{"id":"LE102-3dcbb7ba601d3861","title":"Remilitarisation of the Rhineland","kind":"history","reference":"https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?search=Remilitarisation%20of%20the%20Rhineland","aliases":["Remilitarisation of the Rhineland"],"photos":[],"questionIds":["ARCHED-NEW101-0464"],"tapestryIds":["t68-354134bbf702"],"museumIds":[],"mapIds":[],"note":"German troops entered a demilitarised zone, violating treaty commitments."},{"id":"LE102-b5c62946ae6c34d2","title":"Rome–Berlin Axis announced","kind":"history","reference":"https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?search=Rome%E2%80%93Berlin%20Axis%20announced","aliases":["Rome–Berlin Axis announced"],"photos":[],"questionIds":["ARCHED-NEW101-0523"],"tapestryIds":["t68-589e592f1c48"],"museumIds":[],"mapIds":[],"note":"A political alignment preceded later military agreements."},{"id":"LE102-b36886afca8850d3","title":"Fallingwater","kind":"architecture","reference":"https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?search=Fallingwater","aliases":["Fallingwater"],"photos":[{"src":"/.netlify/functions/access?action=media&name=887e350d5f1144b873eca2c6.webp","sourceUrl":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Fallingwater3.jpg","credit":"lachrimae72","license":"CC0","licenseUrl":"http://creativecommons.org/publicdomain/zero/1.0/deed.en","width":960,"height":630,"file":"File:Fallingwater3.jpg"}],"questionIds":["ARCHED-B100-20261007-013","ARCHED-NEW101-0190","ARCHED-NEW101-0246","ARCHED-NEW101-0247","ARCHED-NEW101-0248","ARCHED-NEW101-0434","ALPHA-B004-Q349","ALPHA-B009-Q830","PDF34-Q-155-A","PDF35-Q072-A","PDF35-CON-009-A"],"tapestryIds":["t68-8af007d3fa69"],"museumIds":[],"mapIds":[],"note":"A Pennsylvania house combining cantilevered concrete terraces with its waterfall setting; guest-house works continued later.","built":"1936","creator":"Frank Lloyd Wright","city":"Mill Run","style":"Organic architecture","era":"Interwar period"},{"id":"LE102-f7e991555b398bf3","title":"Spanish Civil War","kind":"history","reference":"https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?search=Spanish%20Civil%20War","aliases":["Spanish Civil War"],"photos":[],"questionIds":["ALPHA-B009-Q849","NEWDER-014"],"tapestryIds":["t68-11998f56e0a2"],"museumIds":[],"mapIds":[],"note":"Republicans and Nationalists fought with foreign involvement; Franco's victory established a dictatorship."},{"id":"LE102-620f4419be660355","title":"Guernica","kind":"art","reference":"https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?search=Guernica","aliases":["Guernica"],"photos":[{"src":"/.netlify/functions/access?action=media&name=36f33fc963b763daef40c8b7.webp","credit":"Pablo Picasso","license":"Copyrighted artwork; reproduction from Wikipedia. Commercial-use permission not established.","sourceUrl":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:PicassoGuernica.jpg","caption":"Reproduction of Picasso's painting, 1937; original in the Museo Reina Sofía, Madrid."}],"questionIds":[],"tapestryIds":["t68-efbe491b849d"],"museumIds":[],"mapIds":[],"note":"Painted after the bombing of Guernica during the Spanish Civil War, for the Spanish Republic's Paris pavilion.","creator":"Pablo Picasso"},{"id":"LE102-e3dd9ecaf888f4d8","title":"Italy joins the Anti-Comintern Pact","kind":"history","reference":"https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?search=Italy%20joins%20the%20Anti-Comintern%20Pact","aliases":["Italy joins the Anti-Comintern Pact"],"photos":[],"questionIds":["ARCHED-NEW101-0532"],"tapestryIds":["t68-4d99ffc71ad5"],"museumIds":[],"mapIds":[],"note":"Italy joined Germany and Japan in an anti-communist pact; distinguish from the 1940 Tripartite Pact."},{"id":"LE102-e9a1ad02f08a9ddb","title":"Italy leaves the League of Nations","kind":"history","reference":"https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?search=Italy%20leaves%20the%20League%20of%20Nations","aliases":["Italy leaves the League of Nations"],"photos":[],"questionIds":["ARCHED-NEW101-0501"],"tapestryIds":["t68-ccd1bab3bd1d"],"museumIds":[],"mapIds":[],"note":"The withdrawal followed international conflict over its invasion of Ethiopia."},{"id":"LE102-e96d57fca095fde6","title":"Montserrat","kind":"art","reference":"https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?search=Montserrat","aliases":["Montserrat"],"photos":[{"src":"/.netlify/functions/access?action=media&name=6970547ac1ee9eeb06470a17.webp","credit":"Julio González · official artist catalogue","license":"Image rights retained by source; commercial reuse not cleared","sourceUrl":"https://juliogonzalez.org/en/catalogue/la-montserrat-the-montserrat/","caption":"La Montserrat, 1936–1937; full sculpture, not one of the later head or mask studies."}],"questionIds":[],"tapestryIds":["t68-c16b790766e0"],"museumIds":[],"mapIds":[],"no